  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing Component Logic**\n\nI\'m currently fleshing out the components, specifically focusing on `IdleHomeStep.tsx`. I\'m integrating the display for the current address and safe station count as a summary, using `\302\267` as a separator. I\342\200\231m also tackling the display of three nearby 24/7 locations, a key feature.\n\n\n**Refining Step Navigation**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the step components. I\'ve defined tappable rows for safe stations, ensuring they\'re accessible. I\'ve designed the issue selection step, focusing on quick, intuitive buttons, precise label matching to the mock data options, and back/next button placement for one-thumb use. I\'m also adding a short note input for when \"Kh\303\241c\" is selected.\n\n\n**Defining Step Functionality**\n\nI\'m focusing now on the second step. I\'ve designed two distinct options: staying put at the current address (with visual confirmation) or moving to the nearest safe station. The key is that the mechanic\'s pickup address updates instantly on station selection, shown right above the \"X\303\241c nh\341\272\255n g\341\273\215i c\341\273\251u h\341\273\231\" CTA, with a loading spinner to Step 3. I\'m also planning the tracking step to handle searching, accepted and completed states, focusing on a clear flow for each state.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
