  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visual Validation**\n\nI\'m incredibly impressed by the visual validation. The absence of console errors throughout the journey is a huge win, but seeing those mobile screenshots (\"r1-step1.png\", \"r1-step2.png\", \"r1-step3-accepted.png\", \"r1-step3-completed.png\") truly solidifies the value.\n\n\n**Pinning Bottom Sheet Actions**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the top defects found during visual polish, specifically in the mobile flow. The most critical involves an overflow and CTA pinning issue in Step 2. The fix involves structuring the bottom sheet to keep primary action buttons sticky at the bottom while the middle content scrolls, directly aligning with design principles. This also impacts similar issues in Step 1.\n\n\n**Refining Mobile UI Details**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into mobile UI specifics, especially Step 2, focusing on the bottom sheet\'s layout to keep the CTA consistently visible without scrolling. The goal is a crisp, uncluttered experience. I\'m also tweaking the maximum height to accommodate the 3-station picker, ensuring both options and the sticky CTA feel optimal on smaller screens.\n\n\n**Adjusting Display Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on subtle UI refinements. The map pin text clipping on mobile and desktop required a max-width adjustment for full visibility of the petrol station name. I also addressed the cramped right edge of the \"Demo\" button on mobile by tweaking the padding and text size to ensure a clean visual appearance. Finally, I fixed a text wrapping issue on the completed card by implementing shrink-0 and text alignment fixes.\n\n\n**Optimizing Visual Consistency**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on font and layout inconsistencies. The progress bar labels in the bottom sheet required adjustments, specifically, Vietnamese text needed a `font-sans` with `font-medium` for readability, while numbers stayed with `font-mono tabular-nums`. I\'m applying this change to `BottomSheetShell.tsx` and refining the mobile display using this font standard with extra tweaks in `TopOverlayBar.tsx` for a cleaner fit and `NightMapView.tsx` for station labels, and refining mechanic markers. I am also adjusting the font on top overlay to fit mobile.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
