  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Discovering Core Issue**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed the root cause for the visual discrepancies. The camera\'s misalignment in `r4-mobile-idle.png` and `r4-mobile-step2-route.png`, along with the canvas issue, stems from the order of operations in both the Playwright test script and React. Specifically, how the page initially loads.\n\n\n**Analyzing Viewport Impacts**\n\nI\'ve discovered the viewport\'s default size caused the initial `useEffect` to trigger a `map.flyTo` with desktop padding, and, crucially, MapLibre GL *persists* the right padding value. This means that when Playwright subsequently resizes the viewport, the persisted padding becomes incompatible with the new, narrower width, resulting in the negative horizontal space issue. This causes elements like Circle K to be shifted to the left. The root cause comes from the interplay of map initialisation padding settings, their persistence in maplibregl, and viewport resizing.\n\n\n**Investigating FitBounds Errors**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"Map cannot fit within canvas\" error from `fitBounds`. I suspect either map resize persistence or a failure of the map to resize itself before or after the `fitBounds` call. It seems that the map might be incorrectly persisting asymmetric right padding across viewport changes. I\'m focusing on the interaction of container dimensions, viewport resizing, and the application of responsive padding through `map.setPadding()`. I\'m going to add a `ResizeObserver` to the container to handle responsive padding updates.\n\nI will ensure to compute `bottomPadding` responsively.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_6061508662768128847"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"\'use client\';\\n\\nimport { Map as MapLibreMap, Marker, setWorkerUrl } from \'maplibre-gl\';\\nimport \'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css\';\\nimport maplibreWorkerUrl from \'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs?url\';\\nimport { useEffect, useRef, useState } from \'react\';\\nimport type {\\n  GeoCoord,\\n  GeoJsonLineString,\\n  MechanicInfo,\\n  PickupMode,\\n  RescueStep,\\n  SafeStation,\\n  TrackingStatus,\\n  UserLocation,\\n} from \'../types/rescue\';\\nimport { computeBoundsBox } from \'../utils/rescueLogic\';\\nimport {\\n  ensureRescueRouteLayers,\\n  setRouteSourceGeometry,\\n} from \'./map/mapLayers\';\\nimport {\\n  createMechanicMarkerElement,\\n  createStationMarkerElement,\\n  createUserMarkerElement,\\n} from \'./map/mapMarkers\';\\nimport { StationPreviewCard } from \'./map/StationPreviewCard\';\\n\\nsetWorkerUrl(maplibreWorkerUrl);\\n\\nconst CARTO_DARK_STYLE_URL =\\n  \'https://basemaps.cartocdn.com/gl/dark-matter-gl-style/style.json\';\\n\\nfunction getViewportPadding(container: HTMLDivElement | null, forRoute: boolean) {\\n  const width = container?.clientWidth ?? window.innerWidth;\\n  const height = container?.clientHeight ?? window.innerHeight;\\n  if (width >= 1024) {\\n    return forRoute\\n      ? { top: 80, bottom: 80, left: 60, right: Math.min(480, Math.round(width * 0.42)) }\\n      : { top: 40, bottom: 40, left: 40, right: Math.min(440, Math.round(width * 0.4)) };\\n  }\\n  const safeBottom = forRoute\\n    ? Math.min(380, Math.max(220, Math.round(height * 0.52)))\\n    : Math.min(340, Math.max(200, Math.round(height * 0.46)));\\n  return { top: forRoute ? 80 : 48, bottom: safeBottom, left: 40, right: 40 };\\n}\\n\\ninterface RescueMapProps {\\n  userLocation: UserLocation;\\n  stations: SafeStation[];\\n  selectedStationId: string | null;\\n  inspectedStationId: string | null;\\n  pickupMode: PickupMode;\\n  pickupCoord: GeoCoord;\\n  walkingRoute: GeoJsonLineString | null;\\n  step: RescueStep;\\n  trackingStatus: TrackingStatus;\\n  mechanic: MechanicInfo;\\n  mechanicCoord: GeoCoord;\\n  recenterSignal: number;\\n  onSelectStation: (stationId: string) => void;\\n  onInspectStation: (stationId: string | null) => void;\\n}\\n\\nexport function RescueMap({\\n  userLocation,\\n  stations,\\n  selectedStationId,\\n  inspectedStationId,\\n  pickupMode,\\n  pickupCoord,\\n  walkingRoute,\\n  step,\\n  trackingStatus,\\n  mechanic,\\n  mechanicCoord,\\n  recenterSignal,\\n  onSelectStation,\\n  onInspectStation,\\n}: RescueMapProps) {\\n  const containerRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement | null>(null);\\n  const mapRef = useRef<MapLibreMap | null>(null);\\n  const userMarkerRef = useRef<Marker | null>(null);\\n  const stationMarkersRef = useRef<Marker[]>([]);\\n  const mechanicMarkerRef = useRef<Marker | null>(null);\\n  const [mapReady, setMapReady] = useState(false);\\n\\n  const inspectedStation =\\n    stations.find((s) => s.id === inspectedStationId) ?? null;\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const el = containerRef.current;\\n    if (!el || mapRef.current) return;\\n\\n    const map = new MapLibreMap({\\n      container: el,\\n      style: CARTO_DARK_STYLE_URL,\\n      center: [userLocation.coord.lng, userLocation.coord.lat],\\n      zoom: 15.2,\\n      attributionControl: false,\\n      pitchWithRotate: false,\\n      dragRotate: false,\\n    });\\n\\n    map.on(\'load\', () => {\\n      ensureRescueRouteLayers(map);\\n      map.easeTo({\\n        center: [userLocation.coord.lng, userLocation.coord.lat],\\n        padding: getViewportPadding(el, false),\\n        duration: 0,\\n      });\\n      setMapReady(true);\\n    });\\n\\n    const observer = new ResizeObserver(() => {\\n      map.resize();\\n    });\\n    observer.observe(el);\\n    mapRef.current = map;\\n\\n    return () => {\\n      observer.disconnect();\\n      stationMarkersRef.current.forEach((m) => m.remove());\\n      stationMarkersRef.current = [];\\n      userMarkerRef.current?.remove();\\n      mechanicMarkerRef.current?.remove();\\n      map.remove();\\n      mapRef.current = null;\\n      setMapReady(false);\\n    };\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const map = mapRef.current;\\n    if (!map) return;\\n\\n    userMarkerRef.current?.remove();\\n    const isSearching = step === \'tracking\' && trackingStatus === \'searching\';\\n    const el = createUserMarkerElement(isSearching);\\n    userMarkerRef.current = new Marker({ element: el })\\n      .setLngLat([userLocation.coord.lng, userLocation.coord.lat])\\n      .addTo(map);\\n  }, [userLocation.coord.lat, userLocation.coord.lng, step, trackingStatus]);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const map = mapRef.current;\\n    if (!map || !mapReady) return;\\n    map.flyTo({\\n      center: [userLocation.coord.lng, userLocation.coord.lat],\\n      zoom: 15.2,\\n      padding: getViewportPadding(containerRef.current, false),\\n      duration: 600,\\n    });\\n  }, [userLocation.coord.lat, userLocation.coord.lng, recenterSignal, mapReady]);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const map = mapRef.current;\\n    if (!map) return;\\n\\n    stationMarkersRef.current.forEach((marker) => marker.remove());\\n    stationMarkersRef.current = stations.map((station) => {\\n      const isHighlighted =\\n        inspectedStationId === station.id ||\\n        (selectedStationId === station.id &&\\n          (step === \'pickup\' || step === \'tracking\') &&\\n          pickupMode === \'safe_station\');\\n\\n      const el = createStationMarkerElement(station, isHighlighted, () => {\\n        onInspectStation(station.id);\\n        onSelectStation(station.id);\\n      });\\n\\n      return new Marker({ element: el, anchor: \'top\' })\\n        .setLngLat([station.coord.lng, station.coord.lat])\\n        .addTo(map);\\n    });\\n  }, [stations, selectedStationId, inspectedStationId, step, pickupMode]);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const map = mapRef.current;\\n    if (!map || !mapReady) return;\\n\\n    setRouteSourceGeometry(map, \'walking-route\', walkingRoute);\\n    if (!walkingRoute) return;\\n\\n    const bounds = computeBoundsBox(walkingRoute.coordinates);\\n    if (bounds) {\\n      map.resize();\\n      map.fitBounds(bounds, {\\n        padding: getViewportPadding(containerRef.current, true),\\n        duration: 600,\\n        maxZoom: 16.5,\\n      });\\n    }\\n  }, [walkingRoute, mapReady]);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const map = mapRef.current;\\n    if (!map || !mapReady) return;\\n\\n    const showMechanic =\\n      step === \'tracking\' &&\\n      (trackingStatus === \'accepted\' || trackingStatus === \'completed\');\\n\\n    mechanicMarkerRef.current?.remove();\\n    mechanicMarkerRef.current = null;\\n\\n    if (!showMechanic) {\\n      setRouteSourceGeometry(map, \'mechanic-route\', null);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    const isCompleted = trackingStatus === \'completed\';\\n    const currentPos = isCompleted ? pickupCoord : mechanicCoord;\\n    const el = createMechanicMarkerElement(\\n      mechanic.name,\\n      mechanic.etaMinutes,\\n      isCompleted,\\n    );\\n\\n    mechanicMarkerRef.current = new Marker({ element: el, anchor: \'bottom\' })\\n      .setLngLat([currentPos.lng, currentPos.lat])\\n      .addTo(map);\\n\\n    setRouteSourceGeometry(map, \'mechanic-route\', {\\n      type: \'LineString\',\\n      coordinates: [\\n        [mechanicCoord.lng, mechanicCoord.lat],\\n        [pickupCoord.lng, pickupCoord.lat],\\n      ],\\n    });\\n  }, [step, trackingStatus, mechanicCoord, pickupCoord, mechanic, mapReady]);\\n\\n  return (\\n    <section\\n      aria-label=\\\"B\341\272\243n \304\221\341\273\223 th\341\273\261c t\341\272\277 khu v\341\273\261c v\303\240 Tr\341\272\241m An To\303\240n 24/7\\\"\\n      data-testid=\\\"rescue-map-canvas\\\"\\n      className=\\\"relative h-full w-full bg-slate-950\\\"\\n    >\\n      <div ref={containerRef} className=\\\"h-full w-full\\\" />\\n\\n      {inspectedStation && step === \'idle\' && (\\n        <div className=\\\"pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 top-16 z-20 px-4\\\">\\n          <div className=\\\"pointer-events-auto relative mx-auto max-w-md lg:mx-0\\\">\\n            <StationPreviewCard\\n              station={inspectedStation}\\n              onClose={() => onInspectStation(null)}\\n            />\\n          </div>\\n        </div>\\n      )}\\n    </section>\\n  );\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Add ResizeObserver and responsive container-based padding in RescueMap so mobile Bottom Sheet never covers user pin or OSRM walking route\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/RescueMap.tsx\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating RescueMap responsive camera padding\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update src/components/RescueMap.tsx\"}"
