  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Key Visuals**\n\nI\'m currently focused on comparing visuals, specifically `r5-mobile-step2-route.png` and `r5-desktop-step3.png`. I noticed in `r5-mobile-idle.png`, the user\'s blue dot, \"Circle K L\303\252 Th\303\241nh T\303\264n\", and \"FamilyMart Pasteur\" are cleanly centered in the upper half. This observation sparked an interest in layout variations.\n\n\n**Analyzing Padding Values**\n\nI\'ve uncovered the root cause for \"C\303\264ng an Ph\306\260\341\273\235ng B\341\272\277n Ngh\303\251\" being off-screen in `r5-mobile-step2-route.png`. It boils down to conflicting padding values set by `map.flyTo` and `map.fitBounds`. The initial `flyTo` call sets a base padding. Then, `fitBounds` *adds* its padding on top of the existing one, resulting in excessive bottom padding and the station being hidden. I\'m confirming the exact math:  `340 (stored in transform.padding.bottom) + 380 (options.padding.bottom) = 720`!!\n\n\n**Fixing Padding Overflows**\n\nI\'ve got it! The issue stems from MapLibre GL\'s `flyTo` mutating the `map.transform.padding`, which `fitBounds` then *adds* its own padding to. This causes padding to overflow canvas bounds, triggering an error. My solution? Consistently reset padding to zero with `map.setPadding({ top: 0, bottom: 0, left: 0, right: 0 })` before invoking `flyTo` and `fitBounds`.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_2373060334112845944"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Reset MapLibre transform padding before easeTo, flyTo, and fitBounds so padding never stacks across camera calls\", \"EndLine\":182, \"Instruction\":\"Call map.setPadding({ top: 0, bottom: 0, left: 0, right: 0 }) before easeTo, flyTo, and fitBounds in RescueMap.tsx\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"    map.on(\'load\', () => {\\n      ensureRescueRouteLayers(map);\\n      map.setPadding({ top: 0, bottom: 0, left: 0, right: 0 });\\n      map.easeTo({\\n        center: [userLocation.coord.lng, userLocation.coord.lat],\\n        padding: getViewportPadding(el, false),\\n        duration: 0,\\n      });\\n      setMapReady(true);\\n    });\\n\\n    const observer = new ResizeObserver(() => {\\n      map.resize();\\n    });\\n    observer.observe(el);\\n    mapRef.current = map;\\n\\n    return () => {\\n      observer.disconnect();\\n      stationMarkersRef.current.forEach((m) => m.remove());\\n      stationMarkersRef.current = [];\\n      userMarkerRef.current?.remove();\\n      mechanicMarkerRef.current?.remove();\\n      map.remove();\\n      mapRef.current = null;\\n      setMapReady(false);\\n    };\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const map = mapRef.current;\\n    if (!map) return;\\n\\n    userMarkerRef.current?.remove();\\n    const isSearching = step === \'tracking\' && trackingStatus === \'searching\';\\n    const el = createUserMarkerElement(isSearching);\\n    userMarkerRef.current = new Marker({ element: el })\\n      .setLngLat([userLocation.coord.lng, userLocation.coord.lat])\\n      .addTo(map);\\n  }, [userLocation.coord.lat, userLocation.coord.lng, step, trackingStatus]);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const map = mapRef.current;\\n    if (!map || !mapReady) return;\\n    map.setPadding({ top: 0, bottom: 0, left: 0, right: 0 });\\n    map.flyTo({\\n      center: [userLocation.coord.lng, userLocation.coord.lat],\\n      zoom: 15.2,\\n      padding: getViewportPadding(containerRef.current, false),\\n      duration: 600,\\n    });\\n  }, [userLocation.coord.lat, userLocation.coord.lng, recenterSignal, mapReady]);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const map = mapRef.current;\\n    if (!map) return;\\n\\n    stationMarkersRef.current.forEach((marker) => marker.remove());\\n    stationMarkersRef.current = stations.map((station) => {\\n      const isHighlighted =\\n        inspectedStationId === station.id ||\\n        (selectedStationId === station.id &&\\n          (step === \'pickup\' || step === \'tracking\') &&\\n          pickupMode === \'safe_station\');\\n\\n      const el = createStationMarkerElement(station, isHighlighted, () => {\\n        onInspectStation(station.id);\\n        onSelectStation(station.id);\\n      });\\n\\n      return new Marker({ element: el, anchor: \'top\' })\\n        .setLngLat([station.coord.lng, station.coord.lat])\\n        .addTo(map);\\n    });\\n  }, [stations, selectedStationId, inspectedStationId, step, pickupMode]);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const map = mapRef.current;\\n    if (!map || !mapReady) return;\\n\\n    setRouteSourceGeometry(map, \'walking-route\', walkingRoute);\\n    if (!walkingRoute) return;\\n\\n    const bounds = computeBoundsBox(walkingRoute.coordinates);\\n    if (bounds) {\\n      map.resize();\\n      map.setPadding({ top: 0, bottom: 0, left: 0, right: 0 });\\n      map.fitBounds(bounds, {\\n        padding: getViewportPadding(containerRef.current, true),\\n        duration: 600,\\n        maxZoom: 16.5,\\n      });\\n    }\\n  }, [walkingRoute, mapReady]);\", \"StartLine\":89, \"TargetContent\":\"    map.on(\'load\', () => {\\n      ensureRescueRouteLayers(map);\\n      map.easeTo({\\n        center: [userLocation.coord.lng, userLocation.coord.lat],\\n        padding: getViewportPadding(el, false),\\n        duration: 0,\\n      });\\n      setMapReady(true);\\n    });\\n\\n    const observer = new ResizeObserver(() => {\\n      map.resize();\\n    });\\n    observer.observe(el);\\n