  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\n- **Project**: **MotoSOS Night** (`MotoSOS`) \342\200\224 A mobile-first, dark-mode (`slate-950`) emergency motorbike rescue & 24/7 Safe Station locator web application styled in a clean Xanh SM\342\200\223inspired minimalist aesthetic, built in a React 19 + Vite 8 + Tailwind CSS v4 + TypeScript workspace (dev server on port 3000; note: user mentioned Next.js App Router conventions in prompts, and the applet runs on Vite, so `\'use client\'` and safe `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_GEOAPIFY_KEY` Vite `define` wiring are maintained for compatibility).\n- **Current User Request (Turn 3 refinement)**:\n  1. **Clean Map & No Mock Map**:\n     - Ensure simulated grid map and hardcoded `\"182 \304\220i\341\273\207n Bi\303\252n Ph\341\273\247\"` are completely gone.\n     - Use `maplibre-gl` + `\'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css\'` with CARTO Dark Matter style (`https://basemaps.cartocdn.com/gl/dark-matter-gl-style/style.json`).\n     - Real GPS via `navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition` (fallback `10.7769, 106.7009`) + Geoapify Places API (`process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_GEOAPIFY_KEY`, `lng,lat`, 1500m radius, limit 4) with mock fallback if key missing or empty results.\n     - **Safe Station Markers**: Render on the map **ONLY** as compact circular icon buttons (`w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 border border-emerald-400`), with **NO** text label boxes underneath. Show the station name/details card only when the user clicks directly on that icon.\n  2. **Ultra-Compact Home Screen (`idle` Bottom Sheet \342\211\244 32% viewport height)**:\n     - Keep 68%+ of the upper screen open for the map.\n     - In `IdleHomeStep`, remove the big heading, subtitle, and pre-expanded 3/4-station list. Keep **ONLY 3 elements**:\n       1. Compact current address line (`text-xs text-slate-400 truncate`).\n       2. Prominent amber primary CTA button: `\"G\341\273\214I S\341\273\254A XE KH\341\272\250N C\341\272\244P\"`.\n       3. Quick-select pill button below: `\"T\303\254m Tr\341\272\241m An To\303\240n g\341\272\247n \304\221\303\242y (24/7) \342\206\222\"` (clicking this jumps directly to Step 2 with `safe_station` mode active to show the station list and draw the OSRM walking route).\n  3. **Polish Details**:\n     - Hide browser scrollbars on all scrollable areas using `[&::-webkit-scrollbar]:hidden [-ms-overflow-style:none] [scrollbar-width:none]`.\n     - Shrink top overlay bar: compact `\"MotoSOS\"` logo on the left and tiny `\"Test th\341\273\243\"` button (`text-xs px-2.5 py-1.5`) on the right so it never covers map markers.\n- **Constraints**:\n  - Every source file in `src/` MUST remain strictly under **250 lines**.\n  - Active skills already loaded in conversation context: `ultra-mode`, `frontend-design` (with `references/10_mobile_touch_apps.md`), and `computer-use` (`playwright-cli`).\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Completed in Earlier Turns (Verified & Working)\n- Workspace & Metadata: `/metadata.json`, `/index.html` (Vietnamese `lang=\"vi\"`, `Plus Jakarta Sans` + `JetBrains Mono`), `/src/index.css` (Tailwind v4 `@custom-variant dark`, compositor-only `@keyframes stepEnter`, `prefers-reduced-motion`).\n- Package Installed: `maplibre-gl` (`^6.18.0`) added via `install_applet_package`.\n- Env & Vite Config: `/.env.example` documents `NEXT_PUBLIC_GEOAPIFY_KEY` & `VITE_GEOAPIFY_KEY`; `/vite.config.ts` sets `envPrefix: [\'VITE_\', \'NEXT_PUBLIC_\']` and `define: { \'process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_GEOAPIFY_KEY\': JSON.stringify(...) }`.\n- Domain & Logic Files (all < 250 lines):\n  - `/src/types/rescue.ts` (59 lines)\n  - `/src/data/mockRescueData.ts` (110 lines) \342\200\224 HCMC fallback `10.7769, 106.7009` (`\"Trung t\303\242m Qu\341\272\255n 1, TP. H\341\273\223 Ch\303\255 Minh\"`) + 4 real-coord mock stations + 4 issues (`L\341\273\247ng l\341\273\221p`, `Ch\341\272\277t m\303\241y`, `H\341\272\277t x\304\203ng`, `Kh\303\241c`) + mechanic mock.\n  - `/src/utils/rescueLogic.ts` (123 lines) \342\200\224 Pickup target resolution, Haversine distance, walking minutes, bounds box, demo status progression (`searching -> accepted -> completed`), `buildMechanicApproachCoord`.\n  - `/src/utils/mapApi.ts` (212 lines) \342\200\224 Geoapify Places API fetch & mapper + OSRM walking route fetch (`router.project-osrm.org/route/v1/foot/...`) with safe fallbacks.\n  - `/src/hooks/useRescueGeo.ts` (134 lines) \342\200\224 Browser geolocation hook, Geoapify station fetch, OSRM walking route fetch.\n  - Unit tests: `/src/utils/rescueLogic.test.ts` (91 lines), `/src/utils/mapApi.test.ts` (49 lines) \342\200\224 10/10 passing via `npx --yes tsx --test`.\n- Map Components & Old File Cleanup:\n  - Deleted obsolete simulated map files `/src/components/NightMapView.tsx` and `/src/components/map/MapBackdropSvg.tsx`.\n  - `/src/components/map/StationPreviewCard.tsx` (46 lines)\n  - `/src/components/RescueMap.tsx` (244 lines) \342\200\224 MapLibre GL with CARTO Dark Matter, explicit `setWorkerUrl(maplibreWorkerUrl)`, `ResizeObserver`, padding reset `map.setPadding({ top: 0, bottom: 0, left: 0, right: 0 })` before camera updates, smart `fitBounds`, clickable station markers, OSRM walking route layer, and mechanic route/marker in Step 3.\n\n### Completed in Current Turn (Turn 3 \342\200\224 Not Yet Re-compiled/Browser-Verified)\n1. `/src/components/map/mapMarkers.ts`: Updated Safe Station markers to render ONLY as compact circular icons (`w-8 h-8 rounded-full border border-emerald-400 bg-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-300 backdrop-blur-sm` inside a `h-11 w-11` button hit target) with ZERO text boxes underneath.\n2. `/src/components/map/mapLayers.ts`: Adjusted `getViewportPadding` idle mobile bottom padding to `Math.min(260, Math.max(180, Math.round(height * 0.32)))` to match the compact 32% Bottom Sheet.\n3. `/src/components/TopOverlayBar.tsx`: Shrunk header cluster to compact `\"MotoSOS\"` left badge and tiny `\"Test th\341\273\243\"` (`text-xs px-2.5 py-1.5`) right button (switching to `\"Xong ca\"` / `\"Th\341\273\255 l\341\272\241i\"` during tracking states).\n4. `/src/components/BottomSheetShell.tsx`: Set `max-h-[32dvh]` when `step === \'idle\'` (and `max-h-[54dvh]` on active steps 1\342\200\2233), keeping the floating circular `\"V\341\273\201 v\341\273\213 tr\303\255 c\341\273\247a t\303\264i\"` button right above the top-right edge (`-top-14 right-4`).\n\n### Remaining / Not Yet Edited for Turn 3\n- `/src/components/steps/IdleHomeStep.tsx` \342\200\224 Still has old heading, subtitle, and 4-station list (needs to be stripped down to the exact 3 requested elements + scrollbar-hiding classes).\n- `/src/components/steps/IssueSelectionStep.tsx`, `/src/components/steps/PickupSelectionStep.tsx`, `/src/components/steps/TrackingStep.tsx` \342\200\224 Need `[&::-webkit-scrollbar]:hidden [-ms-overflow-style:none] [scrollbar-width:none]` on all `overflow-y-auto` containers.\n- `/src/utils/rescueLogic.ts` & `/src/App.tsx` \342\200\224 Need to wire the new `\"T\303\254m Tr\341\272\241m An To\303\240n g\341\272\247n \304\221\303\242y (24/7) \342\206\222\"` quick-action pill button in `IdleHomeStep` to open Step 2 (`pickup`) directly in `safe_station` mode (drawing the OSRM route immediately), handle `\"Quay l\341\272\241i\"` from Step 2 cleanly (return to `idle` if `selectedIssue === null`, else `issue`), and ensure `getIssueLabel` returns `\"C\341\273\251u h\341\273\231 xe m\303\241y kh\341\272\251n c\341\272\245p\"` instead of `\"Ch\306\260a ch\341\273\215n s\341\273\261 c\341\273\221\"` if submitted after coming straight from the Safe Station shortcut without picking an issue.\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **MapLibre GL v6 Worker in Vite 8**: Default MapLibre worker loading fails in Vite dev (`Error: Worker failed to load`) because Vite pre-bundles `maplibre-gl` into `node_modules/.vite/deps/`. Fixed cleanly by importing `maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs?url` (IIFE standalone worker) and calling `setWorkerUrl(maplibreWorkerUrl)` before map initialization, plus using named exports `{ Map as MapLibreMap, Marker, setWorkerUrl } from \'maplibre-gl\'` (no default export).\n- **MapLibre Transform Padding Stacking Bug**: Calling `map.flyTo({ padding })` persists `padding` on `map.transform.padding`. Subsequent `map.fitBounds(bounds, { padding: { top: 80, bottom: 380, ... } })` combines/conflicts with persisted padding on a `390x844` mobile viewport, emitting `[WARNING] Map cannot fit within canvas with the given bounds, padding, and/or offset` and aborting the camera fit. Fixed by calling `map.setPadding({ top: 0, bottom: 0, left: 0, right: 0 })` immediately before `easeTo`, `flyTo`, and `fitBounds`.\n- **`motion/react` Hook Mismatch**: `motion/react` `AnimatePresence` crashed at runtime in Vite + React 19 with `Invalid hook call / Cannot read properties of null (reading \'useContext\')`. Replaced with pure CSS `@keyframes stepEnter` in `/src/index.css` (zero runtime issues, smooth 190ms compositor transition).\n- **Real OSRM API Works Live**: Headless Chromium successfully fetches CARTO Dark Matter vector tiles and real walking routes from `https://router.project-osrm.org/route/v1/foot/...`.\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n1. **`AnimatePresence` Runtime Crash (`TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading \'useContext\')`)**: Replaced `motion/react` transitions with CSS `.animate-step-enter` keyed wrapper in `src/App.tsx` and `src/index.css`.\n2. **`\"default\" is not exported by \"node_modules/maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs\"`**: Switched to named imports `{ Map as MapLibreMap, Marker, setWorkerUrl }` from `\'maplibre-gl\'`.\n3. **`Error: Worker failed to load` in MapLibre**: Added `import maplibreWorkerUrl from \'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs?url\'` and `setWorkerUrl(maplibreWorkerUrl)`.\n4. **`Map cannot fit within canvas with the given bounds, padding, and/or offset` + off-screen mobile route**: Added `ResizeObserver` calling `map.resize()` and reset `map.setPadding({ top: 0, bottom: 0, left: 0, right: 0 })` before every `easeTo`/`flyTo`/`fitBounds` in `RescueMap.tsx`. Resolved to 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n5. **File > 250 lines constraint**: Refactored `NightMapView.tsx`, `App.tsx`, and `RescueMap.tsx` earlier by extracting `useRescueGeo.ts`, `mapLayers.ts`, `mapMarkers.ts`, `StationPreviewCard.tsx`. Always verify all files remain `< 250` lines via `wc -l`.\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- Modified in Turn 3 (not yet compiled/tested): `mapMarkers.ts`, `mapLayers.ts`, `TopOverlayBar.tsx`, `BottomSheetShell.tsx`.\n- Dev server is currently running stale code from Turn 2 until Turn 3 edits finish and `restart_dev_server` is called.\n- No orphaned Chromium processes left open (all `playwright-cli` runs used `trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT`).\n- Notice in `RescueMap.tsx` line 231: `<StationPreviewCard>` only renders when `inspectedStation && step === \'idle\'`. Check whether clicking a circular station icon on the map during `step === \'pickup\'` should also show the station name toast/preview or rely on highlighting in Step 2\'s Bottom Sheet list (currently clicking a marker calls both `onInspectStation(station.id)` and `onSelectStation(station.id)`, so in `idle` it shows `StationPreviewCard` at the top of the map, and in `pickup` it selects that station in the Bottom Sheet and draws the OSRM route; consider also displaying `StationPreviewCard` or keeping current behavior \342\200\224 in `idle` it cleanly displays the station card only when tapped!).\n\n## 6. Next Steps\n1. **Update `/src/components/steps/IdleHomeStep.tsx`**:\n   - Strip title, subtitle, and station list completely.\n   - Render ONLY the 3 requested items inside a compact container (`px-5 pt-2 pb-4`):\n     1. Compact address line (`MapPin` + `text-xs text-slate-400 truncate` showing `userLocation.address`).\n     2. Large amber primary CTA button: `\"G\341\273\214I S\341\273\254A XE KH\341\272\250N C\341\272\244P\"` (`min-h-[50px]`).\n     3. Quick-select pill button underneath (`rounded-full border border-emerald-500/35 bg-slate-950/80 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-medium text-emerald-300`): `\"T\303\254m Tr\341\272\241m An To\303\240n g\341\272\247n \304\221\303\242y (24/7) \342\206\222\"` calling a new `onOpenSafeStations` callback.\n   - Add `[&::-webkit-scrollbar]:hidden [-ms-overflow-style:none] [scrollbar-width:none]` on the inner scrollable wrapper.\n2. **Add scrollbar-hiding classes** (`[&::-webkit-scrollbar]:hidden [-ms-overflow-style:none] [scrollbar-width:none]`) to `overflow-y-auto` containers in:\n   - `/src/components/steps/IssueSelectionStep.tsx`\n   - `/src/components/steps/PickupSelectionStep.tsx`\n   - `/src/components/steps/TrackingStep.tsx`\n3. **Update `/src/utils/rescueLogic.ts` & `/src/utils/rescueLogic.test.ts`**:\n   - Update `getIssueLabel` fallback when `issueId === null` to `\'C\341\273\251u h\341\273\231 xe m\303\241y kh\341\272\251n c\341\272\245p\'` (so going straight from `\"T\303\254m Tr\341\272\241m An To\303\240n g\341\272\247n \304\221\303\242y (24/7) \342\206\222\"` -> Step 2 -> Step 3 works cleanly without requiring Step 1 first), and update unit test accordingly.\n4. **Update `/src/App.tsx`**:\n   - Track `enteredFromQuickStations` boolean (or check `selectedIssue === null`) so:\n     - Clicking `\"T\303\254m Tr\341\272\241m An To\303\240n g\341\272\247n \304\221\303\242y (24/7) \342\206\222\"` sets `pickupMode(\'safe_station\')`, `inspectedStationId(null)`, and `setStep(\'pickup\')`.\n     - Clicking `\"Quay l\341\272\241i\"` in Step 2 returns to `\'idle\'` if `enteredFromQuickStations` (or `!selectedIssue`), else `\'issue\'`.\n     - Reset `enteredFromQuickStations` in `handleResetFlow` and when clicking `\"G\341\273\214I S\341\273\254A XE KH\341\272\250N C\341\272\244P\"`.\n   - Ensure `App.tsx` and every `.ts`/`.tsx` file stays strictly `< 250` lines.\n5. **Run Verification & Audits (After Final Edit)**:\n   - Run unit tests + hardcoded string/size check:\n     - `npx --yes tsx --test src/utils/rescueLogic.test.ts src/utils/mapApi.test.ts`\n     - `find src -type f \\( -name \'*.ts\' -o -name \'*.tsx\' \\) -exec wc -l {} +` (confirm every file `< 250` lines)\n     - Verify `\"182 \304\220i\341\273\207n Bi\303\252n Ph\341\273\247\"` is absent via grep.\n   - Co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet`.\n   - Call `restart_dev_server`.\n   - Run **1 targeted round of `playwright-cli` browser verification** (`ultra-mode` rule for follow-up edits) with `trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT` and unique filenames (e.g. `.playwright-cli/r7-mobile-idle.png`, `.playwright-cli/r7-mobile-station-tap.png`, `.playwright-cli/r7-mobile-step2.png`):\n     - Verify on `390x844`: Home Bottom Sheet \342\211\244 32% height, 68%+ clean CARTO Dark Matter map visible, Safe Stations appear ONLY as `w-8 h-8` circular emerald icons (no text boxes), tapping a station icon opens `StationPreviewCard`, clicking `\"T\303\254m Tr\341\272\241m An To\303\240n g\341\272\247n \304\221\303\242y (24/7) \342\206\222\"` opens Step 2 & draws the OSRM emerald walking route cleanly above the Bottom Sheet, clicking `\"Test th\341\273\243\"` advances tracking state, and console has 0 errors / 0 warnings.\n   - Inspect all captured PNGs visually before finishing and summarize concisely in Vietnamese.\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Language & Style**: Respond to the user in Vietnamese, concise and scannable, without exposing file paths or internal system details in the final user-facing summary.\n- **Ultra-mode Verification Gate**: Do not finish until unit tests, `compile_applet`, `lint_applet`, `restart_dev_server`, and live browser screenshot inspection have ALL passed *after* the last code modification. Never claim checks passed without running them after the final edit.\n- **Line Limit**: Every `.ts`/`.tsx` source file must stay strictly under 250 lines.\n- **Browser Tool Rules**: Always use global `playwright-cli` with `--browser=chromium`, unique `.playwright-cli/*.png` filenames, and `trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT`.\n</summary>"
