  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Initial UI Elements**\n\nOkay, I\'m carefully examining the first screenshot, `r7-mobile-idle.png`. The UI is indeed clean. I noted the compact \"MotoSOS\" badge and the unobtrusive \"Test th\341\273\243\" button on the top bar. There\'s no overlap, which is great. Now I will move to the Map!\n\n\n**Evaluating Map and Bottom Sheet**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the CARTO Dark Matter map, which covers most of the screen. I see a blue user dot with a soft halo and four emerald icons without text. The Bottom Sheet is within the target height. The three requested items are clearly displayed: the address, amber CTA, and a pill for nearby safe stations. I\'ve also noted the floating recenter button\'s position.\n\n\n**Revising Height Calculations**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a discrepancy between calculated and observed bottom sheet heights. Specifically, the hardcoded `-h-[54dvh]` value (around 455px on an 844px screen) in the UI appears taller than the `safeBottom` calculated in `mapLayers.ts`, which is capped at 380px. This led me to think the calculated `safeBottom` was smaller than expected, pushing the UI elements and route underneath the expected bottom sheet size! I\'m planning to revisit `getViewportPadding` and adjust the calculation so it considers `Math.round(height * 0.56)` to prevent clipping issues. I also noticed a discrepancy with OSRM and will investigate that further in `mapApi.ts`.\n\n\n"
