  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Discovering OSRM\'s Quirks**\n\nI\'ve made a key discovery about `router.project-osrm.org`. The public demo server unexpectedly defaults to car routing, even when the intended profile is pedestrian. This is a crucial observation, impacting our understanding of OSRM\'s public demo\'s behavior. It seems the `/route/v1/foot/` endpoint is the only real \"foot\" routing option on the public demo.\n\n\n**Refining Walking Estimates**\n\nI\'ve realized a significant improvement for walking time estimation using `estimateWalkingMinutes(dist)`, which avoids the car-centric default on the public OSRM server, as it guarantees realistic speeds (~75m/min). Plus, I\'ve corrected the `getViewportPadding` calculation to accommodate the Bottom Sheet and ensure clear route visibility, especially on mobile. The RescueMap.tsx fix will make the route and mechanic markers visible during tracking too!\n\n\n"
