  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Planning the Redesign**\n\nI\'m in the thick of redesign planning, meticulously considering every user detail and the `ultra-mode` verification plan. I\'ve begun mapping out the screens, starting with the mobile interface. My focus is on ensuring a smooth transition based on the user\'s specific request, and all features within the ultra-mode.\n\n\n**Designing the New Layout**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics, starting with the outer shell. I envision a smartphone frame on desktops with the dimensions `1440x900` centered against a dark background. On smaller screens like `390x844`, it\'ll be edge-to-edge. I\'m prioritizing a clean, scrollbar-free experience, a critical design choice. Next, I\'m focusing on the first tab, \"Trang ch\341\273\247\" (Home). It\'ll be a clean white canvas with a clear header, a hero action bar, and a grid of icons for quick access to driver actions. I\'m focusing on the \"S\341\273\261 c\341\273\221\" (Issues) column, and on the compact \"An to\303\240n 24/7\" badge.\n\n\n**Refining the Workflow**\n\nI\'m now refining the workflow for issue selection and mapping integration. Clicking an issue like \'Ch\341\272\277t m\303\241y\' directly opens the \"B\341\272\243n \304\221\341\273\223\" tab, with the issue pre-selected. I\'m debating the cleanest approach: pre-selecting at Step 1 or Step 2. I\'m leaning toward pre-selection at Step 1, highlighting the chosen issue. For \'K\303\255ch b\303\254nh\', I\'m considering mapping it to \'engine_dead\' with a custom note. I am digging into how all of this integrates.\n\n\n**Clarifying the Mapping**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the issue mapping strategy, focusing on integrating \"K\303\255ch b\303\254nh\" (battery jump) seamlessly. I\'ve decided to add `\'battery_jump\'` to `IssueType` and `ISSUE_OPTIONS`, ensuring consistent handling. I\'ll maintain the existing options (`L\341\273\247ng l\341\273\221p`, `Ch\341\272\277t m\303\241y`, `H\341\272\277t x\304\203ng`, `K\303\255ch b\303\254nh`) and incorporate a \"Kh\303\241c\" option for comprehensive coverage in the `IssueSelectionStep`. This ensures smooth pre-selection from the home grid and bottom sheet interactions.\n\n\n**Defining the Issue Selection**\n\nI\'m now nailing down the issue pre-selection logic for the \"B\341\272\243n \304\221\341\273\223\" tab. The core is clear: clicking any of the four grid items on Row 1 should open the \"B\341\272\243n \304\221\341\273\223\" tab with the corresponding issue pre-selected. After re-reading the requirements, it\'s clear the design targets pre-selection at Step 1 (`issue`), presenting the highlighted option with a ready-to-use \"Ch\341\273\215n \304\221i\341\273\203m ch\341\273\235 th\341\273\243\" button. This offers a one-tap process, with the option to add a note. Showing Step 2 with a compact badge and the ability to go back to Step 1 offers an interesting alternative.\n\n\n**Integrating the Issue Display**\n\nI\'ve decided to show the selected issue in both Step 1 (highlighted) and the Step 2 header for maximum clarity. The `battery_jump` addition to `IssueType` and `ISSUE_OPTIONS` ensures seamless integration and doesn\'t break any current unit tests.\nI\'ve also started working on integrating the new \"Tr\341\272\241m an to\303\240n\" (Safe Station) options. Clicking `C\341\273\255a h\303\240ng 24/7`, `C\303\242y x\304\203ng`, or `C\303\264ng an` will open the \"B\341\272\243n \304\221\341\273\223\" tab at Step 2 with the nearest station selected. Finally, I\'m making `G\341\273\255i SOS` open the \"B\341\272\243n \304\221\341\273\223\" tab at Step 2 (`current_location`) with the `selectedIssue = \'other\'` and a note of `\"SOS\"`.\n\n\n**Implementing Night Safety Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating critical safety features for night use. I\'m focusing on the \"SOS\" rescue flow, ensuring a one-tap confirmation for drivers in distress. I\'ve designed a rounded emerald banner with safety tips and a scrollable \"Safe Station Near You\" section powered by Geoapify data, directly linking to a map tab.\n\n\n**Analyzing Map Integration**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the map integration, with walking routes in emerald. Key detail: the container width inside the map tab *must* be considered at `max-w-[430px]` and the height above bottom nav (`h-16`) to ensure correct viewport padding, for route display. I\'m focusing on ensuring the recenter button and bottom sheet are properly placed.\n\n\n**Refining the Workflow**\n\nI\'m now integrating the tracking flow. Step 3 includes real-time tracking with simulated driver acceptance and a button within the header. Tabs 3 (\"Ho\341\272\241t \304\221\341\273\231ng\") and 4 (\"An to\303\240n\") will be dynamically useful, reflecting actual app state. The \"Ho\341\272\241t \304\221\341\273\231ng\" tab displays active rescue trips and history, while \"An to\303\240n\" provides night safety tips and nearby safe stations.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Navigation**\n\nI\'ve just finalized the bottom navigation bar. It\'s fixed to the bottom of the `430px` mobile shell, with four tabs: `Trang ch\341\273\247`, `B\341\272\243n \304\221\341\273\223`, `Ho\341\272\241t \304\221\341\273\231ng`, and `An to\303\240n`. Each has a clear emerald-600 active state, 22px icons, and 11px labels, ensuring easy navigation.\n\n\n**Structuring the Architecture**\n\nI\'m now focusing on file organization to keep things clean. I\'m updating `index.html` with body classes for styling. I\'ve also begun to build out the `src` folder, including CSS, TypeScript types for rescue data with the `battery_jump` issue, and adding mock data, and I\'m ensuring everything stays under 250 lines per file.\n\n\n**Organizing the Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating new components and refining existing ones. I\'m adding `SAFETY_BANNER_SLIDES`, `SAFETY_CHECKLIST_ITEMS`, `EMERGENCY_CONTACTS`, and `INITIAL_ACTIVITY_HISTORY` to `ISSUE_OPTIONS`. I\'ve added a helper function, `findStationByCategory()`, in `/src/utils/rescueLogic.ts` and its test, ensuring that clicking on the safe station grid options now correctly finds the nearest station from the mock/Geoapify data. I\'ve finished the bottom navigation bar and the basic structures for each tab, focusing on a clean home screen, the activity tab, and the safety tab. I\'m working on the rescue map and also switching style URLs.\n\n\n**Adapting the Light Theme**\n\nI\'m now adapting the map display to CARTO Positron with a light map container and adjusting `StationPreviewCard`. I\'m updating map markers, and designing a light-mode floating header, and a light-mode bottom sheet shell.\n\n\n\n**Designing Light Mode**\n\nI\'m now implementing the light mode. I\'m focusing on the circular recenter button\'s styling and designing a light mode for various components. These include: the map-tab idle bottom sheet in `/src/components/steps/IdleHomeStep.tsx`, the light mode issue grid in `/src/components/steps/IssueSelectionStep.tsx`, the light mode pickup cards with an emerald CTA in `/src/components/steps/PickupSelectionStep.tsx`, and light mode tracking cards with an inline \"Gi\341\272\243 l\341\272\255p th\341\273\243 nh\341\272\255n \304\221\306\241n\" button in the tracking step in `/src/components/steps/TrackingStep.tsx`. Lastly, I\'m integrating these components within a mobile-first shell in `/src/App.tsx`.\n\n\n"
