  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Updating Map View Components**\n\nI\'m currently focused on transitioning the RescueMap component to a clean, light mode aesthetic, inspired by the Xanh SM style. Specifically, I\'m updating the CARTO style in `/src/components/RescueMap.tsx` to utilize the `https://basemaps.cartocdn.com/gl/positron-gl-style` basemap. This change sets the stage for a uniform, brighter visual experience across the application\'s map interface.\n\n\n**Refining UI Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now diving into the finer details of the UI\'s light mode. I\'m focusing on `/style.json` for canvas adjustments and `bg-slate-100` elements for a consistent look. I\'m also implementing a clean, white floating bar in `/src/components/TopOverlayBar.tsx` for the \"B\341\272\243n \304\221\341\273\223\" tab, including a compact layout for buttons. Furthermore, I\'m working on a light Bottom Sheet in `/src/components/BottomSheetShell.tsx` and refining the appearance of components such as step progress bars, and the \"V\341\273\201 v\341\273\213 tr\303\255 c\341\273\247a t\303\264i\" button. I am also currently working on cleaning up `/src/components/steps/IdleHomeStep.tsx` and `/src/components/steps/IssueSelectionStep.tsx`, ensuring white backgrounds and emerald accents.\n\n\n**Implementing Rescue Flows**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the rescue flows, specifically focusing on the `/src/components/steps` directory. I\'m building out clean, white components with emerald accents, starting with pickup and tracking steps. I\'m implementing card layouts and CTAs that offer high-contrast and an integrated visual experience. I\'m concurrently tackling the root `App.tsx` file to wire up all components, incorporating live activity updates and essential integrations. I plan to iterate through these steps in parallel for accelerated development.\n\n\n"
