  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visuals Rigorously**\n\nI\'m scrutinizing the screenshots, adopting a discerning product designer\'s perspective. The visuals appear strong initially, yet I\'m looking for defects or areas that could be improved, considering their overall refinement and authenticity. I\'m focusing on the first two screenshots, *r9-desktop-home.png* and *r9-mobile-home.png*, to begin the critique.\n\n\n**Evaluating Mobile Layout**\n\nI\'m now diving into the mobile design specifics. The `r9-mobile-home.png` screenshot reveals a strong, authentic app feel with the centered white smartphone frame and clean header. The hero pill bar is effective, and the pastel icon grid is well-executed. I\'m also finding the Geoapify Safe Stations integration and fixed bottom navigation to be user-friendly. I\'ve noted a couple of small polish opportunities in `r9-mobile-map.png`, specifically concerning the OSRM route and the bottom sheet.\n\n\n**Refining Mobile Map**\n\nI\'ve been examining specific mobile map details. I\'ve pinpointed an opportunity to improve the route visibility in `r9-mobile-map.png` by tweaking the `safeBottom` calculation in `mapLayers.ts`. I also considered the text layout of the bottom sheet. Specifically, the line of text in `r9-mobile-map.png` feels tight on narrow screens. Finally, I\'m happy with how the map looks. Next, I plan to run a full verification.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_6511661342738954808"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Increase route bottom padding slightly so OSRM southern bends stay completely above the 58% white Bottom Sheet\", \"EndLine\":99, \"Instruction\":\"Adjust forRoute safeBottom ratio in mapLayers.ts from 0.56 to 0.61\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"  const safeBottom = forRoute\\n    ? Math.min(Math.round(height * 0.61), Math.max(220, height - 180))\\n    : Math.min(240, Math.max(160, Math.round(height * 0.34)));\", \"StartLine\":92, \"TargetContent\":\"  const safeBottom = forRoute\\n    ? Math.min(Math.round(height * 0.56), Math.max(200, height - 180))\\n    : Math.min(240, Math.max(160, Math.round(height * 0.32)));\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/map/mapLayers.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Adjusting route bottom padding in mapLayers.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Adjust route bottom padding\"}"
