  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Uncovering the Dependency**\n\nI\'ve just pinpointed something significant. Examining `/node_modules/motion/package.json`, specifically lines 78-80, reveals that `\"motion\": \"12.43.0\"` relies on `\"framer-motion\": \"^12.43.0\"`. I also see that `motion/react` re-exports from `framer-motion`. I\'m considering adding `resolve: { dedupe: [\'` to my configuration.\n\n\n**Refining the Approach**\n\nI\'ve decided to leverage `motion/react` directly, as it\'s the declared dependency. Adding `dedupe: [\'react\', \'react-dom\']` in `vite.config.ts` will prevent Vite from bundling duplicate React copies, ensuring a consistent environment. I\'m keen to test this setup immediately in Chromium to verify its effectiveness.\n\n\n**Optimizing UI Layout**\n\nI\'m focusing on UI layout, particularly for the `BottomNavBar`. I\'m going to make the `BottomNavBar` `absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 z-30` with frosted glass. This lets content scroll smoothly behind it. I\'m also ensuring the bottom cards scroll well clear above the bottom nav with `pb-28`. On `MapTabView`, `BottomSheetShell` will sit `bottom-16`. I think this ensures the bottom nav never overlaps map controls.\n\n\n**Designing the Bottom NavBar**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the design of the `BottomNavBar`, aiming for a frosted glass effect using `border-slate-200/60` and positioning it absolutely at the bottom with `inset-x-0 bottom-0 z-30`. I\'m using `pb-28` for scrollable tabs to prevent overlap. I\'m choosing `bottom-16` on `BottomSheetShell` within `MapTabView` to ensure the map extends beneath the nav bar with actions right above. I also have added `mapLayers.ts` safeBottom update.\n\n\n**Refining Layout Strategy**\n\nI\'m now implementing the layout refinements. Setting `mb-16` on `MapTabView` ensures the container height for `RescueMap` is precise. This provides full-bleed scrolling behind the frosted-glass `BottomNavBar` for `HomeTab`, `ActivityTab`, and `SafetyTab`, incorporating `pb-28` to prevent overlap. I\'m also now adding some `@keyframes` in `src/index.css` for shimmer and sheen effects to build some micro-interactions. Specifically, I am using `motion.div` with variants for staggered entrance on `HomeTab`.\n\n\n**Designing the Rescue Tab**\n\nI\'m now designing the Rescue Tab. It will feature a full-width border with an emerald glow. On the left will be a pulsing emerald radar dot, and on the right, a call-to-action pill with a shimmer effect that responds to taps. I\'m also implementing eight squircle icons in a grid with gradients, inner highlights, and spring animations for press. I am building a \"VIP Night Shield\" banner as well.\n\n\n**Enhancing Visuals**\n\nI\'m now implementing the \"VIP Night Shield\" banner. I\'m focusing on a deep emerald-to-slate gradient background. I\'ve included a translucent glowing shield watermark. I\'m also adding a subtle light sheen effect that cycles every 4.5 seconds across three night safety tips, using an animated progress bar.\n\n\n\n**Implementing the Indicator**\n\nI\'m now incorporating a frosted glass `BottomNavBar` with an emerald indicator pill that slides smoothly using `layoutId=\"navIndicator\"`. I\'m using `motion.span` with a spring transition, specifically checking Chromium to avoid any React 19 layout group issues.\n\n\n"
