  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Aligning Layout Dimensions**\n\nI\'m currently focused on ensuring perfect pixel alignment between the `HomeTab.tsx` and `NearbyStationsCarousel.tsx` components. Specifically, I\'m examining the padding discrepancies, namely the difference between `px-4` and `px-5`, and how these values relate to the full-bleed calculations. My immediate attention is on the `HomeTab.tsx` inner wrapper\'s current padding values: `px-4 pt-4 pb-28`.\n\n\n**Optimizing Flush Alignment**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously refining the pixel-perfect alignment between `HomeTab.tsx` and `NearbyStationsCarousel.tsx`. The core issue was padding discrepancies. Specifically, I realized that updating `HomeTab.tsx`\'s inner padding from `px-4` to `px-5` resolves the negative margin overflow. This guarantees a clean, flush viewport alignment. The added benefit is that the resulting `20px` padding then mirrors the Apple Maps/Xanh SM \"breathing room,\" for a much cleaner layout!\n\n\n**Implementing Scroll Snapping**\n\nI\'m now integrating scroll functionality and iOS scroll snap into `NearbyStationsCarousel.tsx`, coupled with dynamic pagination dots. I devised a pure index computation helper in `rescueLogic.ts` for this purpose. I unit-tested this to compute the active carousel index. Specifically, the container now has `snap-x snap-mandatory scroll-smooth` and the right padding is handled with `scroll-pl-5`.\n\n\n**Refining Scroll Interactions**\n\nI\'m currently addressing a lag issue between programmatic scroll and desktop drag-to-scroll when using `scroll-smooth`. My solution involves toggling `scroll-smooth` off during dragging with `isDragging ? \'scroll-auto cursor-grabbing\' : \'scroll-smooth cursor-grab\'`! This provides instant mouse tracking during the drag, yet maintains smooth snapping after releasing. Additionally, I\'m ensuring each card uses `snap-start`, without altering the internal card markup. I\'m also implementing refs to manage drag state more robustly.\n\n\n**Managing Drag State**\n\nI\'m currently refining the drag-to-scroll functionality. I\'ve introduced refs for critical drag state variables: `startScrollLeftRef`, `isPointerDownRef`, and `didDragRef`. My `onMouseMove` handler now calculates `dx` and adjusts the scroll position, toggling `isDragging`. I\'m using `didDragRef` to prevent accidental card clicks after dragging, ensuring proper click behavior in these cases. I\'m also addressing race conditions arising from synchronous click events post `mouseup`.\n\n\n**Finalizing Carousel Integration**\n\nI\'ve just added dynamic pagination dots beneath the carousel for enhanced navigation, which updates the `activeIndex` on scroll. I\'ve centered these dots below the carousel using flexbox, handling active and inactive states with `bg-emerald-500` and `bg-slate-300`, respectively. Clicking a dot now smoothly scrolls the carousel to the corresponding card. Additionally, I\'ve implemented a robust click suppression mechanism using `onClickCapture` to prevent unwanted click events after a drag, which handles the race conditions.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_5285608604373907392"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Add computeActiveCarouselIndex pure helper to rescueLogic.ts\", \"EndLine\":184, \"Instruction\":\"Append computeActiveCarouselIndex to rescueLogic.ts\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"  const first = normalizeStreet(parts[0]);\\n  if (parts.length === 1) return first;\\n\\n  const last = normalizeDistrict(parts[parts.length - 1]);\\n  if (last.toLowerCase() === first.toLowerCase()) return first;\\n  return `${first}, ${last}`;\\n}\\n\\nexport function computeActiveCarouselIndex(\\n  scrollLeft: number,\\n  maxScrollLeft: number,\\n  itemCount: number,\\n  cardStepPx = 274,\\n): number {\\n  if (itemCount <= 1) return 0;\\n  if (maxScrollLeft > 0 && scrollLeft >= maxScrollLeft - 4) {\\n    return itemCount - 1;\\n  }\\n  const index = Math.round(Math.max(0, scrollLeft) / cardStepPx);\\n  return Math.min(itemCount - 1, Math.max(0, index));\\n}\\n\", \"StartLine\":174, \"TargetContent\":\"  const first = normalizeStreet(parts[0]);\\n  if (parts.length === 1) return first;\\n\\n  const last = normalizeDistrict(parts[parts.length - 1]);\\n  if (last.toLowerCase() === first.toLowerCase()) return first;\\n  return `${first}, ${last}`;\\n}\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/utils/rescueLogic.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Adding carousel index helper to rescueLogic.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Add computeActiveCarouselIndex helper\"}"
