  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining File Structure**\n\nI\'m focusing on crafting a modular file structure for `src/`. My goal is to keep every file under 250 lines, ideally between 80-210. This is to ensure separation of concerns: pure logic, custom hooks, and UI components. The breakdown starts with `/src/types/rescue`. I\'m prioritizing clarity and maintainability.\n\n\n**Refining Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve been updating the `src/types/rescue.ts` file. Specifically, I\'ve added a `VoucherOption` with types for discount codes, and an `OrderPricing` interface. I have also added a `ChatMessage` interface to enable user-mechanic communications. Further, I have added an optional field `finalPriceLabel` to `RescueActivityItem`.\n\n\n**Updating Fixed Pricing**\n\nI\'ve just added detailed, fixed pricing options to `ISSUE_OPTIONS`, specifying amounts for each rescue scenario. This includes localized titles and subtitles. I\'ve also incorporated a `VOUCHER_OPTIONS` array, with discount codes like \"ANTOAN20\" and \"DEMKHUYA15,\" each with specific requirements and descriptions. I\'m focusing on ensuring these vouchers integrate cleanly into the ordering process.\n\n\n**Implementing New Logic**\n\nI\'ve added new discount vouchers, like \'BANMOI25\', with specific discount amounts and descriptions. Also, I\'ve integrated `QUICK_CHAT_SUGGESTIONS` with helpful phrases for user interaction. Finally, I\'ve updated the mock mechanic\'s phone number to match the `tel:` link. I\'m also splitting utility functions to keep modules under target length. Notably, I\'ve updated `buildMechanicApproachCoord` in `rescueLogic.ts` to ~1.3km from pickup.\n\n\n**Calculating Rescue Pricing**\n\nI\'ve just finished up several pricing-related utility functions in `src/utils/pricingAndSimLogic.ts`. I\'ve added `formatVnd` to handle Vietnamese currency formatting deterministically, regardless of locale, using regex. I\'ve also implemented `isVoucherEligible` and `calculateRescuePricing` to apply discounts and compute final prices. I\'m focusing on ensuring accurate calculations and integration with voucher logic.\n\n\n**Refactoring Map API**\n\nI\'m now separating OSRM API calls out of `mapApi.ts` to keep the file size down. I\'m moving `fetchWalkingRoute` and `fetchMechanicDrivingRoute` to `osrmApi.ts`. I want to ensure both files stay under 160 lines for readability. I am also working on re-exporting the functions so existing imports and tests won\'t break.\n\n\n**Implementing Mechanic Movement**\n\nI\'m currently working on `useMechanicSimulation.ts` to manage the mechanic\'s movement during the tracking phase. I\'m focusing on fetching the actual OSRM driving route using `fetchMechanicDrivingRoute`, which I\'ve refactored previously. I\'m also implementing the route resampling logic, aiming for a smooth arrival animation. My goal is to advance `stepIndex` to display the movement of the mechanic to the user.\n\n\n**Refining Order State**\n\nI\'m now integrating new state and logic into `useRescueOrderState.ts`. I\'ve added `selectedVoucherId` to manage voucher selection, and automatically clear the \"ANTOAN20\" voucher if the pickup mode changes. I am exposing `pricing` for detailed calculations, and setting flat tire as default if there\'s no selected issue. I\'m also implementing a 1.5s automatic reply timer for chat messages. I\'m stopping movement cleanly on arrival.\n\n**Updating Map Styles**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the visual style of the map layers for a better user experience. In `/src/components/map/mapLayers.ts`, I\'ve added a white \"mechanic-route-casing\" with width of 7 and updated the \"mechanic-route-line\" color to amber-500. These stylistic upgrades are intended to improve clarity.\n\n\n**Enhancing Map Markers**\n\nI\'m now overhauling the map markers for a richer user experience. Specifically, I\'ve added a custom motorbike icon badge for the mechanic marker in `mapMarkers.ts`, complete with a contrasting ring and live ETA update. In `RescueMap.tsx`, I\'m incorporating the mechanic route and ETA, ensuring the map dynamically zooms to frame both the mechanic and the pickup location. My goal is to enhance visual clarity and responsiveness.\n\n\n**Implementing Mechanic Movement**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a smooth mechanic journey visualization. The goal is a mechanic marker that moves with smooth animations along the route. I\'m prioritizing clear and straightforward package prices for the user. I\'ve also incorporated a well-structured billing detail display in `PickupSelectionStep.tsx`.\n\n\n**Refining UI Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the visual display and user interaction elements. I am updating the \"PickupSelectionStep.tsx\" UI. Specifically, I\'m integrating the voucher selection UI. I\'ve designed a voucher drawer displaying available discounts with eligibility hints. I\'m also ensuring the \"Confirm Rescue\" button accurately reflects the discounted total and displays crossed-out original prices. The bottom sheet\'s max height is adjusted for better invoice display.\n\n\n**Finalizing Tracking Step**\n\nI\'m currently finalizing the UI in `TrackingStep.tsx`. I\'ve implemented a dynamic ETA header, updated with `liveEtaMinutes`, and the mechanic info card is now complete with name, rating, license plate, vehicle model, and confirmed package prices. I\'ve also added \"G\341\273\215i \304\221i\341\273\207n\" and \"Nh\341\272\257n tin\" action buttons for user interaction. I\'ve built the `MechanicChatDrawer.tsx` to handle in-app chat with the mechanic, and 3 new quick replies for direct communication.\n\n\n**Refactoring Component Size**\n\nI\'m now focusing on reducing the line count in `TrackingStep.tsx` and `PickupSelectionStep.tsx` to maintain readability. I\'m extracting and refactoring components. I\'ve separated the AcceptedMechanicView and OrderInvoiceAndVoucherBar into their own files. These new files will be `AcceptedMechanicCard.tsx` and `OrderInvoiceBar.tsx`. My goal is to keep these steps under 180 lines. I\'m also implementing the new chat logic, including quick-reply buttons and message display.\n\n\n"
