  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refactoring Map API**\n\nI\'m currently streamlining `mapApi.ts`. I plan to simplify it by re-exporting `fetchWalkingRoute` and `fetchMechanicDrivingRoute` from `./osrmApi`, aiming for a clean reduction to about 160 lines. Concurrently, I\'m developing unit tests in `src/utils/pricingAndSimLogic.test.ts` to ensure everything functions correctly after the changes.\n\n\n**Developing Mechanic Simulation**\n\nI\'m now focused on building the mechanic simulation hook, specifically `useMechanicSimulation.ts`. I\'m carefully reviewing its logic, inputs, state variables, and effects.  I plan to integrate it with the rescue logic, and I intend to ensure that the distance assertions are correct. Currently, I am focused on the effect triggered when the step is \'tracking\' and the tracking status is either \'accepted\' or \'completed\', and am working through the logic needed to fetch and manage the mechanic\'s route.\n\n\n**Refining Route Logic**\n\nI\'m currently working to streamline the route logic within the simulation hook. Specifically, I\'m adjusting how the route progresses based on different tracking statuses. I\'m focusing on the conditions and side effects that must be managed to correctly handle waypoint progression and live ETA updates. I need to ensure that the ETA and coordinates displayed are accurate at all times, based on the current step and tracking status. The objective is to make all these updates cleanly on order resets or completions, focusing on clarity.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_8423217593955461307"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Re-export OSRM route helpers from osrmApi so mapApi stays concise and backward-compatible\", \"EndLine\":210, \"Instruction\":\"Replace inline fetchWalkingRoute with re-exports from ./osrmApi\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"export {\\n  fetchMechanicDrivingRoute,\\n  fetchWalkingRoute,\\n  type RouteFetchResult,\\n} from \'./osrmApi\';\", \"StartLine\":154, \"TargetContent\":\"export async function fetchWalkingRoute(\\n  fromCoord: GeoCoord,\\n  toCoord: GeoCoord,\\n  signal?: AbortSignal,\\n): Promise<{\\n  geometry: GeoJsonLineString;\\n  distanceMeters: number;\\n  durationMinutes: number;\\n  source: \'osrm\' | \'fallback\';\\n}> {\\n  const url = `https://router.project-osrm.org/route/v1/foot/${fromCoord.lng},${fromCoord.lat};${toCoord.lng},${toCoord.lat}?overview=full&geometries=geojson`;\\n\\n  try {\\n    const response = await fetch(url, { signal });\\n    if (response.ok) {\\n      const data = (await response.json()) as {\\n        routes?: Array<{\\n          geometry?: GeoJsonLineString;\\n          distance?: number;\\n          duration?: number;\\n        }>;\\n      };\\n      const firstRoute = data.routes?.[0];\\n      if (\\n        firstRoute?.geometry?.type === \'LineString\' &&\\n        Array.isArray(firstRoute.geometry.coordinates) &&\\n        firstRoute.geometry.coordinates.length >= 2\\n      ) {\\n        const dist = Math.round(firstRoute.distance ?? 0);\\n        const mins = estimateWalkingMinutes(dist);\\n        return {\\n          geometry: firstRoute.geometry,\\n          distanceMeters: dist,\\n          durationMinutes: mins,\\n          source: \'osrm\',\\n        };\\n      }\\n    }\\n  } catch {\\n    // Fallback to direct segment below\\n  }\\n\\n  const fallbackDist = computeHaversineMeters(fromCoord, toCoord);\\n  return {\\n    geometry: {\\n      type: \'LineString\',\\n      coordinates: [\\n        [fromCoord.lng, fromCoord.lat],\\n        [toCoord.lng, toCoord.lat],\\n      ],\\n    },\\n    distanceMeters: fallbackDist,\\n    durationMinutes: estimateWalkingMinutes(fallbackDist),\\n    source: \'fallback\',\\n  };\\n}\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/utils/mapApi.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Simplifying mapApi.ts to re-export OSRM route helpers\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update src/utils/mapApi.ts\"}"
