  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Inspecting Chromium Screenshots**\n\nI\'m carefully examining those four real Chromium screenshots, and they\'ve already revealed two subtle polish bugs that I wouldn\'t have caught with unit tests or DOM checks. The first is a medium-severity copy typo in the Auto-Reply feature.\n\n\n**Fixing UI Text, Clipping**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the auto-reply text in screenshot #4, spotting the repeated \"kho\341\272\243ng\" \342\200\223 a quick typo fix is in progress. The quick chat chips at the bottom of the drawer are also being addressed. They were being cut off and not clearly displayed. I\'m investigating how using `flex-wrap` will make them all instantly visible.\n\n\n**Analyzing Route Geometry**\n\nI\'m thrilled with the OSRM route in `r14-step3-osrm-route.png`. The amber route is crisp and fits well, even with the pickup and motorbike marker. However, I\'ve noticed a significant issue: the mechanic\'s location is across the Saigon River, causing the route to detour unnecessarily. Placing the mechanic in District 1/3 (1.3km NW/W) would drastically improve this.\n\n\n**Verifying New Route Distance**\n\nI\'ve just validated that moving the pickup to the updated coordinates (`lat + 0.0078, lng - 0.0088`) keeps the OSRM route within District 1/3, avoiding the river crossing and using existing streets, which is far better. Haversine distance calculations confirm this adjustment is approximately 1.3km, staying within the urban street grid.\n\nI\'m now checking defect #4 in `r14-step1-prices.png`, card 5. The scrolling looks fine, though reducing min-height and setting line clamp looks good on quick visual inspection.\n\n\n**Refining Component Edits**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that a `gap-1.5` style works well in the confirm button and that adding a space or an `aria-label` is a nice touch. I\'ve also identified three precise, surgical edits. I\'m focusing on the code updates now. This includes removing the duplicate word in `buildMechanicAutoReply`, changing the overflow style in the `MechanicChatDrawer` to `flex-wrap` and also updating the mechanic approach coordinates to avoid the river.\n\n\n"
