    thinking: "**Verifying Expected Behavior**\n\nI\'m now diving into `src/utils/rescueLogic.ts` to examine `getNextDemoTrackingStatus`. Specifically, I\'m verifying the scenario where `current` is \'arrived\'. In that case, I expect `getNextDemoTrackingStatus(\'arrived\')` to resolve to \'completed\', and I\'m cross-referencing lines 88-93 within the `rescue` file for verification.\n\n\n**Confirming Edge Cases**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that both `\'accepted\'` and `\'arrived\'` now cleanly map to `\'completed\'` in `getNextDemoTrackingStatus`, resolving a potential edge case. I\'ve updated `src/utils/rescueLogic.ts` to reflect this. I am now working on modifications in `src/components/map/mapMarkers.ts` to correctly center the mechanic marker, ensuring that it is always pinned to the correct location. Specifically, I\'m adjusting the icon\'s positioning and handling the arrival status message.\n\n\n**Refining Simulation Logic**\n\nI\'m currently focused on `MechanicSimulation.ts`, overhauling the simulation\'s core logic. The old interval and waypoint resampling are gone! I\'m now caching the mechanic driving route from `fetchMechanicDrivingRoute` upon order acceptance. I\'m also capturing route start time and initial ETA. I\'ve introduced a `liveEtaMinutes` state that\'s updated within the 60fps loop. I\'m ensuring chat functionality persists across different tracking statuses. Finally, `handleMechanicArrived` is in `src/hooks/useRescueOrderState.ts`.\n\n\n**Implementing Route Animation**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in `src/hooks/useRescueMapMechanicOverlay.ts`. The focus is on animating the mechanic\'s movement smoothly at 60fps. I\'m ensuring the mechanic marker only appears after validating that a driving route exists with at least two coordinates. The calculation of the cumulative profile and locking the marker initially to the starting coordinate are underway. I\'ve successfully implemented `requestAnimationFrame` and am calculating elapsed time, progress, and sampling the route to update the mechanic\'s position in real-time.\n\n\n**Finalizing Mechanic Animation**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the mechanic animation within `useRescueMapMechanicOverlay.ts`. The road disappears perfectly, keeping the start of the yellow line fixed to the marker\'s center. I\'m calculating the `nextEta` and only updating it if it\'s different from the last notified ETA. This triggers `updateMechanicMarkerElement` and `onEtaMinuteChange`. Once progress reaches 1, the route disappears, the marker badge updates, `onMechanicArrived` fires once, and the animation loop stops. I also ensure the route is cleared and the marker pinned when the tracking status is \'arrived\' or \'completed\'.\n\n\n"
