    thinking: "**Defining Clean Architecture**\n\nOkay, I\'m aiming for a very clean architecture here. The goal is to ensure every requirement functions smoothly and deterministically. I\'m focusing on keeping file sizes below 250 lines, which is a major design constraint. My primary focus right now is establishing domain types in `/src/types/rescue.ts`.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Types**\n\nI\'ve added `MapLayerFilter` with options `\'all\'`, `\'repair_shops\'`, and `\'safe_stations\'`. Additionally, I\'ve defined the `RepairShop` interface, including details like `id`, `name`, `address`, and `distanceMeters`, along with opening hour info and coordinates.\nI\'ve implemented a robust opening hours checker that handles a variety of `opening_hours` strings (from OSM and Geoapify) and correctly parses weekdays and ranges.\n\n\n**Analyzing Time Windows**\n\nI\'m currently focused on precisely interpreting opening hour strings. I\'m handling weekday conversions (e.g., `Tu` to the correct `getDay()` value) and parsing minute ranges within hours. I\'m establishing clear logic for determining if a shop is open or closed, specifically handling explicitly closed scenarios and time window checks. Importantly, I\'m considering cases where `opening_hours` is missing, providing a default \"Open \342\200\242 Call to Confirm\" status. Also, I need to add fallback local mock repair shops for when Geoapify data is unavailable.\n\n\n**Adding Mock Repair Shops**\n\nI\'m now incorporating realistic mock repair shops in Saigon\'s District 1, including 24/7 options and shops with specific daytime hours. This ensures accurate testing of the opening hours filtering logic. I\'m also including a shop with `openingHoursRaw: null` to represent the \"Call to Confirm\" scenario. This comprehensive mock data will thoroughly demonstrate the different states that can be in.\n\n\n**Refining Shop Data**\n\nI\'m now extracting `opening_hours` from both `feature.properties` and `datasource.raw`. I\'ll evaluate these, compute `distanceMeters`, estimate ride time, and format the address concisely. Phone numbers will get handled with fallbacks, and I\'ll sort shops by distance. Also, I\'m integrating the \"closed\" filter and ensuring the list `\"Ti\341\273\207m s\341\273\255a xe (\304\220ang m\341\273\237)\"` only shows open shops.\n\n\n**Clarifying Shop Filtering**\n\nI\'m now refining the logic for the \"T\341\272\245t c\341\272\243\" (All) filter. I\'ve realized that in this view, it makes the most sense to display only the open repair shops and Safe Stations. This helps prevent misleading information to stranded riders, keeping the map focused on active options. I\'ll make sure the filter chip rendering is clean, and the `StationPreviewCard` doesn\'t overlap on the map.\n\n\n**Implementing Filter Interactions**\n\nI\'m now implementing the filter chips for repair shops and safe stations, ensuring they update the `mapFilter` state accurately. I\'m focusing on the visual design, including the horizontal scrolling pills, background effects, and active state highlights. The goal is to provide a clean and intuitive user experience when filtering map markers on the `RescueMap`.\n\n\n**Designing Shop Details**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual details for the repair shop marker and bottom sheet. I\'m designing the hit target button on the map to be 44px with a white wrench icon, and adding a small green dot to indicate open status. Additionally, I\'m working on the bottom sheet that shows when a marker is selected, including a \"back\" button to return to the home screen.\n\n\n**Adding Action Buttons**\n\nI\'m now implementing the action buttons within the shop details. I\'ll include \"D\341\272\253n \304\221\306\260\341\273\235ng\" for route navigation using OSRM, \"G\341\273\215i ti\341\273\207m\" for direct calls, and \"Google Maps\" for external navigation. This will all be presented in a clean, accessible HTML structure without relying on `window.open`. I\'ll also ensure a blue route line on the map.\n\n\n**Integrating Home Tab**\n\nI\'m now integrating a \"Nearby Repair Shops\" section on the home tab, aiming for a concise display of open shops. I\'ll include a header and a compact list, linking to the map tab with the relevant filter. I\'m focusing on a clean visual design, including the name, open status, address, and distance for each shop.\n\n\n**Refactoring Code Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into code refactoring to stay within line count limits. I\'m extracting the BottomSheet content logic to its own file. Also, to maintain line count, I am extracting the repair shop selection and filter chip, and blue route state into a separate hook. I\'m also moving map marker synchronization into its dedicated hook to keep the code under 250 lines.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_14314360893638071145"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"export type AppTab = \'home\' | \'map\' | \'activity\' | \'safety\';\\n\\nexport type IssueType =\\n  | \'flat_tire\'\\n  | \'engine_dead\'\\n  | \'out_of_fuel\'\\n  | \'battery_jump\'\\n  | \'other\';\\n\\nexport type SafeStationCategory = \'convenience\' | \'gas_station\' | \'police\';\\n\\nexport type PickupMode = \'current_location\' | \'safe_station\';\\n\\nexport type RescueStep = \'idle\' | \'issue\' | \'pickup\' | \'tracking\';\\n\\nexport type TrackingStatus = \'searching\' | \'accepted\' | \'arrived\' | \'completed\';\\n\\nexport type VoucherId = \'ANTOAN20\' | \'DEMKHUYA15\' | \'BANMOI25\';\\n\\nexport type MapLayerFilter = \'all\' | \'repair_shops\' | \'safe_stations\';\\n\\nexport interface GeoCoord {\\n  lat: number;\\n  lng: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface SafeStation {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  category: SafeStationCategory;\\n  categoryLabel: string;\\n  address: string;\\n  walkingDistanceMeters: number;\\n  walkingMinutes: number;\\n  openHours: string;\\n  amenities: string[];\\n  coord: GeoCoord;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface RepairShop {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  address: string;\\n  phone: string;\\n  distanceMeters: number;\\n  rideMinutes: number;\\n  openingHoursRaw: string | null;\\n  isOpen: boolean;\\n  openStatusLabel: string;\\n  hasExplicitHours: boolean;\\n  coord: GeoCoord;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface IssueOption {\\n  id: IssueType;\\n  label: string;\\n  subtitle: string;\\n  fixedPrice: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface VoucherOption {\\n  id: VoucherId;\\n  code: VoucherId;\\n  title: string;\\n  description: string;\\n  discountAmount: number;\\n  requiresSafeStation: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface OrderPricing {\\n  basePrice: number;\\n  discountAmount: number;\\n  finalPrice: number;\\n  appliedVoucher: VoucherOption | null;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface ChatMessage {\\n  id: string;\\n  sender: \'user\' | \'mechanic\';\\n  text: string;\\n  timestampLabel: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface MechanicInfo {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  phone: string;\\n  licensePlate: string;\\n  vehicleModel: string;\\n  rating: number;\\n  completedRescues: number;\\n  etaMinutes: number;\\n  distanceKm: number;\\n  coord: GeoCoord;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface UserLocation {\\n  address: string;\\n  district: string;\\n  coord: GeoCoord;\\n  source: \'gps\' | \'fallback\';\\n}\\n\\nexport interface GeoJsonLineString {\\n  type: \'LineString\';\\n  coordinates: [number, number][];\\n}\\n\\nexport interface RescueActivityItem {\\n  id: string;\\n  issueLabel: string;\\n  pickupAddress: string;\\n  mechanicName: string;\\n  licensePlate: string;\\n  timestampLabel: string;\\n  priceLabel?: string;\\n  status: \'completed\' | \'cancelled\';\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Add RepairShop and MapLayerFilter types to rescue domain model\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/types/rescue.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Adding RepairShop and MapLayerFilter types\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update src/types/rescue.ts\"}"
