  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Prioritizing Modular Execution**\n\nI\'m feeling confident about the plan! The clean, modular implementation is proceeding in parallel batches to ensure each `.ts`/`.tsx` file remains concise and compliant. We\'re carefully designing the changes, starting with the `/src/utils/repairShopApi.test` file.\n\n\n**Defining Map Visualizations**\n\nI\'ve moved on to the map-specific components, tackling the visualization details. I\'m adding a \'shop-route\' GeoJSON source with corresponding casing and line layers in `/src/components/map/mapLayers.ts`. Next, I\'m working on the markers, defining the `createRepairShopMarkerElement` function. It includes accessibility considerations with a larger touch target and visual cues for online status and highlighting.\n\n\n**Implementing Map Controls**\n\nI\'m now focused on the map component\'s interactive features. I\'m adding `selectShop`, `navigateToShop`, and `clearShopSelection` functions to manage the user\'s interaction with shop selections and route visualization. The `navigateToShop` will ensure a visually successful route, even if OSRM is unavailable, by falling back to a straight-line route. Also, I\'m working on the user interface, incorporating filter chips at the top of the map, for an intuitive experience.\n\n\n**Refining UI Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user interface refinements. I\'m focusing on the filter chip styling and `RepairShopDetailSheet.tsx` component. For the filter chips, I\'m aiming for a Google Maps-inspired look, making the active pills distinct with a blue or slate background and a crisp dot, while inactive chips have a clean, white feel with a subtle backdrop blur. The detail sheet will be shown in the BottomSheetShell when a shop is selected and the step is idle.\n\n\n**Designing Action Buttons**\n\nI\'ve been working on the action buttons within the shop detail sheet. I\'ve defined three key actions: driving directions with OSRM integration, a direct phone call link that triggers an in-app notice, and a Google Maps search link for alternative navigation. I\'m focusing on a clean design with a compact address and an optional route summary badge, ensuring each button provides clear and direct functionality. I\'m prioritizing loading state for the OSRM route and in-app call notices.\n\n\n**Refining Shop-Sheet Logic**\n\nI\'m making a few tweaks to the bottom sheet. Specifically, I\'m refactoring the layout to ensure the `StationPreviewCard` doesn\'t collide with the filter chips. Also, I\'ve adjusted the `BottomSheetShell` to allow sufficient vertical space for the repair shop detail sheet and step counter. Lastly, I\'ve moved the step switch and `RepairShopDetailSheet` into `MapBottomSheetContent.tsx` to keep `MapTabView.tsx` lean.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_14987221636912803420"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import test from \'node:test\';\\nimport assert from \'node:assert/strict\';\\nimport {\\n  buildGoogleMapsSearchUrl,\\n  formatShopDistanceLabel,\\n  getOpenRepairShops,\\n  mapGeoapifyFeaturesToRepairShops,\\n} from \'./repairShopApi\';\\n\\ntest(\'mapGeoapifyFeaturesToRepairShops evaluates opening_hours and sorts nearest first\', () => {\\n  const userCoord = { lat: 10.7769, lng: 106.7009 };\\n  // 23:00 local time on Wednesday\\n  const lateNight = new Date(2026, 4, 13, 23, 0, 0);\\n\\n  const shops = mapGeoapifyFeaturesToRepairShops(\\n    [\\n      {\\n        geometry: { type: \'Point\', coordinates: [106.702, 10.778] },\\n        properties: {\\n          place_id: \'shop-closed\',\\n          name: \'Ti\341\273\207m \304\220\303\243 \304\220\303\263ng\',\\n          address_line2: \'10 L\303\252 Th\303\241nh T\303\264n, Qu\341\272\255n 1, Ho Chi Minh City\',\\n          distance: 150,\\n          opening_hours: \'Mo-Su 07:00-21:00\',\\n        },\\n      },\\n      {\\n        geometry: { type: \'Point\', coordinates: [106.703, 10.779] },\\n        properties: {\\n          place_id: \'shop-247\',\\n          name: \'S\341\273\255a Xe 24/7\',\\n          address_line2: \'42 L\303\275 T\341\273\261 Tr\341\273\215ng, Qu\341\272\255n 1, Vietnam\',\\n          distance: 320,\\n          opening_hours: \'24/7\',\\n        },\\n      },\\n      {\\n        geometry: { type: \'Point\', coordinates: [106.698, 10.777] },\\n        properties: {\\n          place_id: \'shop-unknown\',\\n          name: \'S\341\273\255a Xe H\341\273\223ng Ph\303\272c\',\\n          address_line2: \'65 Nguy\341\273\205n Du, Qu\341\272\255n 1\',\\n          distance: 280,\\n        },\\n      },\\n    ],\\n    userCoord,\\n    lateNight,\\n  );\\n\\n  assert.equal(shops.length, 3);\\n  assert.equal(shops[0].id, \'shop-closed\');\\n  assert.equal(shops[0].isOpen, false);\\n\\n  const openOnly = getOpenRepairShops(shops);\\n  assert.equal(openOnly.length, 2);\\n  assert.equal(openOnly[0].id, \'shop-unknown\');\\n  assert.equal(openOnly[0].openStatusLabel, \'M\341\273\237 c\341\273\255a \342\200\242 G\341\273\215i x\303\241c nh\341\272\255n tr\306\260\341\273\233c\');\\n  assert.equal(openOnly[1].id, \'shop-247\');\\n  assert.equal(openOnly[1].openStatusLabel, \'\304\220ang m\341\273\237 c\341\273\255a\');\\n  assert.equal(openOnly[1].address, \'42 L\303\275 T\341\273\261 Tr\341\273\215ng, Q.1\');\\n});\\n\\ntest(\'formatShopDistanceLabel and buildGoogleMapsSearchUrl format cleanly\', () => {\\n  assert.equal(formatShopDistanceLabel(450, 2), \'450m \302\267 2 ph\303\272t ch\341\272\241y xe\');\\n  assert.equal(formatShopDistanceLabel(1450, 4), \'1.5 km \302\267 4 ph\303\272t ch\341\272\241y xe\');\\n\\n  const url = buildGoogleMapsSearchUrl({\\n    name: \'S\341\273\255a Xe 24/7\',\\n    address: \'42 L\303\275 T\341\273\261 Tr\341\273\215ng, Q.1\',\\n  });\\n  assert.ok(url.startsWith(\'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=\'));\\n  assert.ok(url.includes(encodeURIComponent(\'S\341\273\255a Xe 24/7 42 L\303\275 T\341\273\261 Tr\341\273\215ng, Q.1\')));\\n});\\n\", \"Description\":\"Add unit tests for repairShopApi opening hours filtering, sorting, distance formatting, and Google Maps link generation\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/utils/repairShopApi.test.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing repairShopApi unit tests\", \"toolSummary\":\"Write repairShopApi tests\"}"
