  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing UX Improvements**\n\nI\'ve been examining the provided screenshots and identified two subtle UX enhancements that, if implemented, would significantly boost the overall user experience to a perfect score. I\'m focusing specifically on the details shown in `r17-map-shops-only.png`, where the \"Ti\341\273\207m s\341\273\255a xe\" filter is active, to pinpoint areas for immediate polish.\n\n\n**Improving Map Interaction**\n\nI\'ve realized the map\'s initial zoom on repair shops is problematic. My solution involves dynamically fitting the map bounds to include the user\'s location and nearby open repair shops when the \"repair_shops\" filter is active. This is something that can be achieved in `RescueMap.tsx`, by automatically invoking `fitMapBoundsSafely` for improved viewport visibility. Another change is being made to the buttons on the `RepairShopDetailSheet`.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Polish**\n\nI\'m now implementing targeted visual improvements. First, I\'ve adjusted the top padding for the route viewport in `/src/components/map/mapLayers.ts` to ensure destination markers never overlap the filter chips. Second, I\'ve styled the action buttons in `/src/components/steps/RepairShopDetailSheet.tsx` for cleaner, single-line rendering. Finally, I\'m working to make the map auto-center on the user\'s location + repair shops when the map first loads.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_3734984697589857636"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Increase top viewport padding for routes so destination pins clear MapFilterChips cleanly\", \"EndLine\":147, \"Instruction\":\"Update top padding for forRoute in getViewportPadding from 72 to 108\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"export function getViewportPadding(\\n  container: HTMLDivElement | null,\\n  forRoute: boolean,\\n) {\\n  const height = container?.clientHeight ?? window.innerHeight;\\n  const safeBottom = forRoute\\n    ? Math.min(Math.round(height * 0.61), Math.max(220, height - 180))\\n    : Math.min(240, Math.max(160, Math.round(height * 0.34)));\\n  return { top: forRoute ? 108 : 52, bottom: safeBottom, left: 36, right: 36 };\\n}\", \"StartLine\":135, \"TargetContent\":\"export function getViewportPadding(\\n  container: HTMLDivElement | null,\\n  forRoute: boolean,\\n) {\\n  const height = container?.clientHeight ?? window.innerHeight;\\n  const safeBottom = forRoute\\n    ? Math.min(Math.round(height * 0.61), Math.max(220, height - 180))\\n    : Math.min(240, Math.max(160, Math.round(height * 0.34)));\\n  return { top: forRoute ? 72 : 52, bottom: safeBottom, left: 36, right: 36 };\\n}\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/map/mapLayers.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Adjusting top route padding in mapLayers.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Increase top route padding\"}"
