  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Map Centering**\n\nI\'ve been poring over `RescueMap.tsx`, specifically lines 181-191. I noticed a crucial detail on line 145: the map is already centered using `userLocation` coordinates within the `map.on(\'load\')` event, a fact that simplifies the logic. I am also investigating whether this is the best possible way, since `userLocation` might not be updated when the `on(\'load\')` is fired.\n\n\n**Refining Centering Logic**\n\nI\'ve refined the logic for map centering. Now, lines 181-191 should only `flyTo` when `recenterSignal` changes or `userLocation.coord` updates *after* the initial load. Crucially, I\'m ensuring it *never* overrides `repair_shops` bounds on the first `mapReady`. I\'m using `useRef` to track `recenterSignal` and `userLocation.coord` changes within a `useEffect` hook. I believe this conditional `flyTo` implementation will lead to a more reliable centering solution.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1048048891240388887"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Prevent initial mapReady flyTo from overriding fitMapBoundsSafely when entering Map tab directly into repair_shops filter\", \"EndLine\":192, \"Instruction\":\"Track prevRecenterRef and prevCoordRef so flyTo runs only on recenterSignal change or live GPS coordinate change\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"  const prevRecenterRef = useRef(recenterSignal);\\n  const prevCoordRef = useRef(userLocation.coord);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const map = mapRef.current;\\n    if (!map || !mapReady) return;\\n\\n    const recenterChanged = prevRecenterRef.current !== recenterSignal;\\n    const coordChanged =\\n      prevCoordRef.current.lat !== userLocation.coord.lat ||\\n      prevCoordRef.current.lng !== userLocation.coord.lng;\\n    prevRecenterRef.current = recenterSignal;\\n    prevCoordRef.current = userLocation.coord;\\n\\n    if (!recenterChanged && !coordChanged) return;\\n    map.setPadding({ top: 0, bottom: 0, left: 0, right: 0 });\\n    map.flyTo({\\n      center: [userLocation.coord.lng, userLocation.coord.lat],\\n      zoom: 15.2,\\n      padding: getViewportPadding(containerRef.current, false),\\n      duration: 600,\\n    });\\n  }, [userLocation.coord.lat, userLocation.coord.lng, recenterSignal, mapReady]);\", \"StartLine\":180, \"TargetContent\":\"  useEffect(() => {\\n    const map = mapRef.current;\\n    if (!map || !mapReady) return;\\n    map.setPadding({ top: 0, bottom: 0, left: 0, right: 0 });\\n    map.flyTo({\\n      center: [userLocation.coord.lng, userLocation.coord.lat],\\n      zoom: 15.2,\\n      padding: getViewportPadding(containerRef.current, false),\\n      duration: 600,\\n    });\\n  }, [userLocation.coord.lat, userLocation.coord.lng, recenterSignal, mapReady]);\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/RescueMap.tsx\", \"toolAction\":\"Fixing flyTo race on mapReady in RescueMap.tsx\", \"toolSummary\":\"Fix flyTo race in RescueMap\"}"
