  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing New Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s new requirements, focusing on the `activeLocation` state. I\'m considering defining `ActiveLocation` and `LocationSuggestion` types within `/src/types/rescue.ts` and synchronizing the `userLocation` from the `activeLocation` to ensure consistency. This should provide a good foundation for integrating the new features.\n\n\n**Implementing Reverse Geocoding**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing reverse geocoding using the Geoapify API. I\'m prioritizing the integration with real GPS data upon app mount, immediately fetching the street address to replace raw coordinates. I\'m also considering doing this for the fallback coordinates, if a Geoapify API key is available. The API key retrieval is already implemented in `src/utils/mapApi.ts`.\n\n\n**Examining API Key Retrieval**\n\nI\'ve taken a close look at the `getGeoapifyApiKey` function in `mapApi.ts`. The implementation prioritizes environment variables as the user suggested (`import.meta.env?.VITE_GEOAPIFY_KEY || process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_GEOAPIFY_KEY`). It\'s a clean and efficient method, and I\'m satisfied with how it handles the API key retrieval.\n\n\n**Refining Clickable Area**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how the button\'s clickable area functions. The main area of the `<button>` will now smoothly open the `LocationSearchModal`. I\'m finalizing the logic for the button\'s text based on the `activeLocation` state. It will dynamically display either the user\'s chosen address or a placeholder. If there\'s no custom location yet, it will default to a prompt.\n\n\n**Designing UI Improvements**\n\nI\'m now focused on refining the user interface, especially the main location selection button. I\'m ensuring it displays the prompt, `\"B\341\272\241n \304\221ang g\341\272\267p s\341\273\261 c\341\273\221 \341\273\237 \304\221\303\242u?\"`, and I\'m updating the HTML, so that the outermost element is a `div`. Inside this, I\'m integrating two sibling buttons: one to trigger the `LocationSearchModal` and the other to initiate the map tab change. I\'m also preparing to design a smooth sliding modal for the location search.\n\n\n**Implementing Modal Functionality**\n\nI\'m now implementing the location search modal, starting with a close button in the header. Below the input, I\'m integrating a quick-select row for \"S\341\273\255 d\341\273\245ng v\341\273\213 tr\303\255 hi\341\273\207n t\341\272\241i c\341\273\247a b\341\272\241n\" with an emerald GPS icon. Clicking this triggers `navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition`, reverse-geocodes with Geoapify, and updates the `activeLocation` state, including setting `isCurrentGPS` to true, before closing the modal. There\'s also a fallback to default coordinates if geolocation fails, ensuring the button always responds. User input will trigger the Geoapify Address Autocomplete API, debounced at 300ms.\n\n\n**Handling Offline Fallbacks**\n\nI\'m now focusing on offline handling and graceful Vietnamese fallbacks. When there\'s no network or in a unit testing environment, I\'ll provide clean, Vietnamese HCMC suggestions that match the search query, which will be styled like Google Maps.  This includes a map pin icon, bold primary titles, compact subtitles, and distance calculations. However, I will always call Geoapify when an API key is present.\n\nAlso, I am auto-refetching rescue geos whenever `activeLocation` changes, looking specifically at `\"Tr\341\272\241m An To\303\240n 24/7\"`.\n\n\n**Coordinating Map Updates**\n\nI\'m now coordinating updates to the map based on the `activeLocation` state. I\'m focusing on the Home tab\'s address display and the horizontal carousel update, including the repair shops list. I\'m ensuring the map camera and user/incident marker are updated correctly, considering scenarios where `activeLocation` changes while on the Home tab. The `RescueMap` is properly initialized with center coordinates, and `flyTo` actions are correctly triggered.\n\n\n**Defining New Geocoding Functions**\n\nI\'m currently working on defining new geocoding functions. I\'m adding `ActiveLocation` and `LocationSuggestion` interfaces to `/src/types/rescue.ts`. I\'m also preparing `/src/utils/geocodeApi.ts` with pure async helpers for reverse geocoding and autocomplete, all utilizing the Geoapify API, including distance formatting and Vietnamese language support. Unit tests will follow in `/src/utils/geocodeApi.test.ts`.\n\n\n**Refining Geocoding Utilities**\n\nI\'m currently focused on refining the helper functions and URL construction for geocoding. I\'m focusing on features such as `parseReverseGeocodeAddress`, `mapAutocompleteFeatures`, and `formatSuggestionDistance` to ensure efficiency. Also, I am adding a method to deal with API key fallback. Next, I am going to upgrade `/src/hooks/useRescueGeo.ts` to manage the `activeLocation` state effectively.\n\n\n\n"
