  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Tracing the User Request**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user request, carefully breaking down each step to map out the initial architecture. My goal is a modular design, ensuring that every file remains concise, ideally under 250 lines. The focus is on clarity and efficiency, and understanding how the \"C\303\242y x\304\203ng\" button trigger impacts the tab change on the map.\n\n\n**Defining API & Filters**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"C\303\242y x\304\203ng\" filter on the map by setting `mapFilter = \'gas_stations\'` and adding a chip to `MapFilterChips`. Simultaneously, I\'m calling an API to scan gas stations around the active location. I\'ve noted that \"C\341\273\255a h\303\240ng 24/7\" and \"C\303\264ng an\" in `HomeActionGrid` must maintain their `handleQuickCategory` functionality, handling the gas station case distinctly.\n\n\n**Implementing API Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the API calls for fetching gas station data. First, I\'m setting up a POST request to Google Places with the necessary headers and a body including the location and radius. In case of failure or if there\'s no Google key, it will fall back to Geoapify. If that also fails, I will use a local seed of real Saigon gas stations. I also plan to compute the exact Haversine distance.\n\n\n**Refining Marker Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on displaying the gas station markers and ensuring the map filter works correctly. I\'m building a system with an orange circular marker using an `Fuel` SVG icon. It\'s designed to highlight when active. My task now is to ensure it only shows when `mapFilter` is set to \'gas_stations\', which should only happen when the user selects a gas station. I\'m also ensuring the map properly fits bounds around the active gas stations. Then I\'m working to include the distance and navigation link on marker click.\n\n\\\nI\'m calculating distances, sorting by walking distance, and marking the nearest station. I\'m building Google Maps direction links with `buildGoogleMapsDirectionsUrl`. Finally, I\'m converting the data to a unified `GasStation` type.\n\n\n**Visualizing Nearby Stations**\n\nI\'m now focused on visualizing the gas station routes. My plan involves drawing clear amber or orange walking/driving routes on the map using MapLibre. I\'m aiming for automatic map bounds fitting to the user\'s location and the selected gas station. I\'m also working on the bottom sheet, adjusting its height to ensure the gas station list is comfortably visible without obscuring the map. I\'m adding a \"Nearest\" indicator and ensuring the list displays key details.\n\n\n**Adding Route Display**\n\nI\'m now integrating the route drawing using OSRM, precisely visualizing walking paths from the user\'s location to each gas station, including an open status and a `ph\303\272t d\341\272\257t b\341\273\231` (walking time) indicator for each station on a bottom sheet. I\'m focusing on \"V\341\272\275 \304\221\306\260\341\273\235ng\" button functionality, which fetches and displays the OSRM route, complete with a loading spinner and active station highlighting. I\'m leveraging `<a href={buildGoogleMapsDirectionsUrl(...)}` for Google Maps integration. I\'ll select the nearest station upon \"\304\220\303\263n t\341\272\241i \304\221\303\242y\" button press.\n\n\n**Refining Voucher Application**\n\nI\'m now refining the voucher application logic for a seamless user experience, especially around the \"\304\220\303\263n t\341\272\241i \304\221\303\242y\" button. My focus is on automatically applying the \'ANTOAN20\' voucher if it\'s not already selected when the user chooses a safe station. I\'m also ensuring the chosen gas station data is correctly managed within the `stations` or `extraSafeStation` data structures, ensuring the exact location is present for smooth pickup target resolution. I\'m aiming for a flow where the user experience feels complete and the activation of the `ANTOAN20` voucher is obvious and seamless.\n\n\n**Validating Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now deeply focused on the data structure logic, especially around safe station pick-up points. I must ensure the \"\304\220\303\263n t\341\272\241i \304\221\303\242y\" functionality works regardless of the initial query. Therefore, I must merge `selectedGasStationOverride` or append `customSafeStation` to `availableStationsForPickup`. I\'m verifying the system can handle scenarios like a user selecting a gas station outside the initial \'safe\' search, setting the `pickupMode`, auto-applying the voucher, and cleanly entering the \'pickup\' stage. I am now planning file structures.\n\n\n**Defining API Functions**\n\nI\'m now defining the API functions and data structures. I\'m updating `MapLayerFilter` and crafting the `GasStation` interface. I\'m building utility functions in `/src/utils/gasStationApi.ts` for Google Maps, Geoapify, and fallback data, including a function to transform the `GasStation` into a `SafeStation` data format. I\'m also preparing for comprehensive unit tests. I am now focused on defining a hook to fetch gas stations on location changes.\n\n\n**Implementing Map UI**\n\nI\'m now implementing the map UI components. I\'m adding a \'gas-route\' source, casing, and line to `/src/components/map/mapLayers.ts`, using white and amber-orange colors. I\'ve built the gas station marker element in `/src/components/map/mapMarkers.ts`, using an amber-colored circle with a Fuel SVG icon and shadow. I\'m adding the \"C\303\242y x\304\203ng\" chip with a Fuel icon to the `MapFilterChips` component, right after \"T\341\272\245t c\341\272\243\" and \"Ti\341\273\207m s\341\273\255a xe\". I\'m also creating a scrollable gas station list for the bottom sheet when the \'gas_stations\' map filter is activated and step is \'idle\', including details like name, distance, address, walking time, and action buttons.\n\n\n**Finalizing Gas Station Markers**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI for visualizing gas stations. I am rendering amber `GasStation` markers when the step is \'idle\' and the filter is set to \'gas_stations\', focusing the map purely on gas stations. I\'m also drawing the gas route and ensuring the map bounds fit around the active location and nearby gas stations, unless a gas route is active. The BottomSheet is adjusted to a maximum height of 48% when the step is idle and gas station or shop details are open.\n\n\n"
