    thinking: "**Wiring the Implementation**\n\nI\'m currently integrating the `useMapPinPicker` hook across the UI, specifically focusing on the `MapBottomSheetContent.tsx` file. I\'m adding clean, optional props for `pinPicker` functionality, ensuring file sizes remain concise. My aim is a robust and manageable implementation.\n\n\n**Refining the Integration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating the `pinPicker` props throughout `MapTabView.tsx`. I\'m aiming for a streamlined object to keep the code concise and readable. I\'m hiding `<MapFilterChips />` during the pin-picking process, and ensuring the `pinPicker` props are passed down correctly to the `<RescueMap />` and `<MapBottomSheetContent />` components, so the process can be coordinated.\n\n\n**Implementing Pin Picker Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating `handleConfirmPinPicker` which processes the pin selection, calling `pinPicker.finishPinPicker()` and updates location using the retrieved coordinates and address. I\'m also addressing cleanup, exporting the necessary functions, and ensuring that `useRescueOrderState.ts` remains under the target line count by carefully managing additions and considering potential line trimming. I will be sure to pass `onStartMapPinPicker` to the `<LocationSearchModal />` component and the `pinPicker` object into the `<MapTabView />`. Also, I\'ll assess the recenter behavior of `RescueMap.tsx` when the map tab is opened from `HomeTab`.\n\n\n"
