  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Calculating Precise Spacing**\n\nI\'ve precisely calculated the `TopOverlayBar` height: 12px padding top, 36px height, and 8px padding bottom, totalling 56px, thus matching `top-14`. My initial concerns about potential overlap with `MapFilterChips` are resolved; the `pointer-events-none` on the header ensures a clean layering. Now, what\'s next?\n\n\n**Prioritizing Chip Hierarchy**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the z-index of the `MapFilterChips`, debating between `z-30` and `z-20`. While `z-20` is currently sufficient, `z-30` offers a more robust guarantee of its display above any potential `StationPreviewCard`, ensuring no visual overlap. Further, I\'m analyzing the `onMouseDown` behavior of chip buttons to understand and mitigate potential drag-related conflicts within the component, testing for horizontal dragging interference by the browser, and ensuring event propagation to prevent unintended side effects on MapLibre GL.\n\n\n**Refining Drag Interaction Logic**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the drag-and-click interaction within the chip component. It\'s a sibling of the container, so propagation stopping isn\'t strictly needed. I\'ve considered scenarios where a user drags over a button, noting the mouse events: `mousedown`, `mousemove`, `mouseup`, and `click`. My logic, including `didDragRef`, appears robust and race-free. I\'ve added a helper function to determine if a move should be treated as a drag, with a threshold of 5px.\n\n\n"
