  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Home Design**\n\nThis home redesign is coming together beautifully! I\'m meticulously reviewing the four parts of the Luxury Super-App Home redesign. My focus is ensuring every requirement is met with polish, modularity (under 250 lines per file), and absolutely no regressions. I\'m taking my time and digging in.\n\n\n**Refining UI Components**\n\nI\'m focused on the UI components now, particularly the Obsidian Dark Header block within `HomeTab.tsx`. The emerald glows are coming along nicely. I\'m also refining the \"MotoSOS Priority\" section with its badge, aiming for visual clarity. The frosted-glass \"Test th\341\273\243\" button\'s styling is under review as well.\n\n\n**Analyzing UI Element Styling**\n\nI\'m deep in the styling details now, specifically focusing on the Search & Quick-Call Bar within the dark header. I\'ve nailed down the backdrop, borders, and rounded corners, and I\'m refining the interactive elements. The CTA button\'s background and hover states are looking good. Also, the elevated floating white card for the 8 action icons is coming together. I\'ve synchronized most icons to the charcoal/smoke-slate palette, keeping the \"L\341\273\247ng l\341\273\221p\" icon accented in emerald.\n\n\n**Defining UI States**\n\nNow, I\'m defining the states for the SOS and other action icons. The SOS button will have a rose background, border, and text, while the remaining icons have a slate color scheme. I\'m focusing on consistency in the UI. Also, I\'ve consolidated data for the campaign banners and perk cards into a dedicated file. I\'m working to implement a full-bleed horizontal scroller with desktop drag-to-scroll functionality for the Peek-a-boo Carousel. Dynamic dot indicators will highlight the current item.\n\n\n**Implementing Banner Styling**\n\nI\'m now implementing the Peek-a-boo Carousel banner styling. I\'ve defined the CSS for a rounded, shadowed card with a dark background and image overlay. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and ensuring a clean visual experience. I\'m also preparing for the banner data, including images, tags, titles, vouchers, and CTAs, and their display requirements.\n\n\n**Finalizing Banner Actions**\n\nI\'m now integrating the banner data and defining the action behaviors. I\'ve mapped the provided image URLs, tags, titles, and CTAs. I\'m focusing on the click actions, specifically the voucher-dependent logic in `useRescueOrderState.ts`. The actions are clearly defined with an implementation plan. I\'ve handled the scenarios where specific vouchers trigger UI updates and navigation changes within the application.\n\n\n**Integrating Banner Interactions**\n\nI\'m now integrating the data and defining interactions. I\'ve set voucher-dependent click actions with logic in `useRescueOrderState.ts`. I\'m handling the cases where vouchers affect UI updates and navigation. Specifically, I\'m setting `selectedVoucherId` to `\'BANMOI25\'` and opening the Map Tab at `\'issue\'`. Additionally, for the fuel rescue banner with `DEMKHUYA15`, I\'m setting `selectedIssue` to `\'out_of_fuel\'`, and opening the Map Tab at `\'pickup\'`, pre-populating with the 65,000\304\221 total. If Banner 4 (\"Xem b\341\272\243ng gi\303\241\") is clicked, the selected voucher and issue are cleared or sets `step` to `\'issue\'` on the Map Tab.\n\nI\'m placing the \"\304\220\341\272\267c Quy\341\273\201n \304\220\341\273\221i T\303\241c 24/7\" section (`PartnerPerksCarousel.tsx`) just below `\"Tr\341\272\241m An To\303\240n g\341\272\247n b\341\272\241n\"` (`NearbyStationsCarousel`) in `HomeTab.tsx`. It\'s a horizontal scroll row with overflow.\n\n\n**Refining Partner Perks**\n\nI\'m now refining the Partner Perks section with its three cards. The styling for each card is set: `w-[195px] shrink-0 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-100 shadow-sm overflow-hidden text-left` with a top image and content below. I\'m focusing on the click actions, specifically the voucher logic in the click behavior for each card. I\'ve considered actions for `\"Circle K x MotoSOS\"`, `\"\304\220\341\272\267c quy\341\273\201n C\341\273\251u H\341\273\231 \304\220\303\252m\"`, and `\"G\303\263i An T\303\242m \304\220\306\260\341\273\235ng D\303\240i\"`.\n\n\n"
