  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Discovering Compact Addresses**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! I checked `rescueLogic.test.ts` and noticed something clever. Specifically, `rescueLogic.ts` contains `formatCompactStationAddress(\'Ly Tu Trong Street, Saigon, Ho Chi Minh City, 71016, Vietnam\')`. The function returns `\'\304\220. Ly Tu Trong, Q.1\'`.\n\n\n**Refining Address Normalization**\n\nI\'ve got it! I realized that when \"Saigon\" is *alone*, like in a shop name, `normalizeRepairShopName` and `formatRepairShopCompactAddress` convert it to \"TP.HCM.\" This keeps the `rescueLogic.ts` tests happy. Now, I\'m checking `NearbyRepairShopsSection.tsx` to align with the prompt, focusing on standardized shop names and compact display.\n\n\n**Designing Home Promotions**\n\nOkay, I\'m making good progress! I\'m creating `homePromotions.ts` with real Unsplash photo URLs for exclusive banners and compact partner perks. The goal is a clean design with precise image choices, voucher IDs, and preselected issues. I\'m also updating `repairShopApi.ts` to include the crucial `normalizeRepairShopName` function, making sure \"Saigon\" consistently becomes \"TP.HCM\" and handles generic repair shop names.\n\n\n**Refining Function Exports**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on the exported functions. I\'m working on `normalizeShopAddress` which combines `formatCompactStationAddress` with a standalone \"Saigon\" replacement. I\'m also refining `formatCompactShopSubline` to present distance and address concisely, including the emerald dot and opening status. The goal is clean, consistent formatting for distance and address.\n\n\n**Constructing Dynamic Carousels**\n\nI\'m deep in the UI now! I\'m creating the `CampaignBannerCarousel.tsx` with a responsive, drag-to-scroll, real-photo carousel, complete with a dark gradient scrim and dynamic pagination. I am also working on `PartnerPerksCarousel.tsx`, featuring compact cards with images, titles, and descriptions. I\'m focusing on ensuring these elements are clean and consistent in design, with CTA button callbacks.\n\n\n**Designing Shop Information**\n\nI\'m focused on presenting shop information clearly! I am building a single-row design for shop cards. I am utilizing a green \"M\341\273\237 c\341\273\255a \342\200\242 G\341\273\215i x\303\241c nh\341\272\255n tr\306\260\341\273\233c\" pill box that\'s compact, featuring a wrench icon and an emerald live dot, along with the shop name and a crisp subline indicating status, distance, and address. I\'m also adding a minimalist circular arrow button. I\'m preparing to update `HomeTab.tsx`, `useRescueOrderState.ts`, and `App.tsx` for a redesign of the home tab header.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
