  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Discovering UX Insights**\n\nI\'ve stumbled upon a fascinating user experience insight! The Playwright error message, specifically \"element is outside of the viewport,\" regarding the Geoapify repair shop marker, is a key piece of information. I\'m focusing on the reasons for this, and the context of the user, to further analyze the UX problem.\n\n\n**Analyzing Viewport Issues**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on why the repair shop marker is outside the viewport, even in \"T\341\272\245t c\341\272\243\" mode. It seems MapLibre\'s initial zoom level in that mode is a key factor, potentially obscuring more distant points. The auto-`fitBounds` logic in `useMapMarkersSync.ts` is also a critical piece of the puzzle, and I need to consider its existing behavior, particularly its previous lack of support for auto-fitting in \'all\' mode. This could be where the problem stems.\n\n\n"
