  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visuals and Metrics**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the screenshots and result metrics, meticulously inspecting every single detail. I\'m especially focused on `verify-map-all.png`, noting the OSRM blue route from the user\'s GPS point to \"S\306\241n S\341\273\255a Xe.\" It\'s incredibly gorgeous, but I must remain critical! I\'m now comparing the provided data.\n\n\n**Investigating Discrepancies in Data**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag. The screenshot clearly displays emerald safe-station pins, yet the telemetry reports `safePins: 0`. It appears the `data-testid` for safe stations might be misidentified. This doesn\'t seem to be a UI problem, as the pins are visible, indicating an issue with how the data is being parsed. I\'m now cross-referencing this finding with other elements in the screenshots.\n\n\n**Observing UI Element Placement**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on UI element placement within the screenshots. I\'m focusing on \"B\306\260\341\273\233c 2 / 3 - Ch\341\273\215n \304\221i\341\273\203m ch\341\273\235,\" and the `MapFilterChips` bar\'s visibility. The `BottomSheetShell` collapse button and the \"B\341\272\241n mu\341\273\221n ch\341\273\235 th\341\273\243 \341\273\237 \304\221\303\242u?\" two-column selector seem clean. The way `Step2PlaceListPicker` is positioned looks very clean too. I\'m now verifying the \"gap\" spacing for the mentioned elements.\n\n\n**Examining Spacing and Data**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the spatial relationship between UI elements in `verify-step2-list.png`. I\'ve noticed a significant gap between `\"Gi\303\241 d\341\273\213ch v\341\273\245 g\341\273\221c\"` and the `Step2PlaceListPicker`, confirming complete separation. The `Step2PlaceListPicker` list displays safe stations such as Circle K, 7-Eleven, and Shop&Go! Then lists the repair shops. The telemetry reports `\"listTelCount\": 8`, confirming 1-tap call links work for all shops in the Step 2 list.\n\n\n"
