  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Crafting The Hook**\n\nI\'m now carefully designing a small hook, `/src/hooks/useCarouselPause.ts`, aiming for under 75 lines. Alternatively, I\'m considering maintaining clean interaction-pause and drag logic so `CampaignBannerCarousel` and `PartnerPerksCarousel` remain compact (under 220 lines each) with consistent 6px drag.\n\n\n**Tracing Event Handlers**\n\nI\'m now tracing every event handler in `useCarouselInteraction`. It includes how I\'ll handle touch and mouse events and manage `isDragging` and `isAutoPausedRef`. The goal is to use `DRAG_THRESHOLD_PX` and `RESUME_DELAY_MS` as constants. I\'m focusing on why a ref is used for `isAutoPausedRef` instead of causing re-renders.\n\n\n**Refining Interaction Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating touch and mouse event handling within `useCarouselInteraction`. Specifically, I\'m defining `resume()`, which clears and sets a timeout. Also, I\'m working on `onTouchStart`, `onTouchEnd`, `onMouseEnter`, `onMouseLeave`, and `onMouseDown` handlers. I\'m taking care to consider how to handle touch-based hover events and manage dragging. Also, I\'m considering implementing logic to ensure dragging finishes if the mouse leaves the component.\n\n\n**Implementing Drag Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `onMouseMove` handler, focusing on smooth dragging and seamless wrapping. I\'m excited about the endless scrolling effect! I\'m carefully considering how to handle dragging past the boundaries using `loopWidth` to wrap the scroll position. It feels great to see it working and the CSS scroll-smooth never lags.\n\n\n**Analyzing Scroll Behavior**\n\nI\'m now focusing on scroll behavior. I\'ve noted how `CampaignBannerCarousel` CSS interacts with `scrollTo` and `isDragging`. Specifically, when dragging, `scroll-smooth` needs to be removed and `snap-x snap-mandatory` temporarily disabled to prevent snapping. I\'ve also identified issues where instant scroll overrides the animation. Now I\'m working on how `isDragging` and `scroll-smooth` interact, paying attention to the instant jump, and `snap-x` behavior. I need to make the logic in a way that provides expected behavior for the user. I\'ll need to expose a `triggerTemporaryPause()` and `consumeDidDrag()` for additional control.\n\n\n**Tracing Glide Logic**\n\nI\'m now tracing the RAF loop for `PartnerPerksCarousel`. Unlike `CampaignBannerCarousel`, the continuous glide uses `requestAnimationFrame` and moves ~0.5px/frame, so I\'m not using `snap-x` or `scroll-smooth` on the container. Currently, I\'m analyzing the `rafId`, `virtualLeft`, and the `step` function to fully understand the smooth continuous movement.\n\n\n**Verifying Continuous Glide**\n\nI\'ve just verified the math behind the continuous glide in `PartnerPerksCarousel`. By adjusting the `deltaPx` based on frame rate, I\'ve maintained the desired visual speed across different screen refresh rates. The `virtualLeft` reset logic ensures seamless, infinite right-to-left scrolling. Now I\'m considering touch/swipe interactions, ensuring clean wrap behavior during pauses or drags to keep the flow uninterrupted.\n\n\n**Analyzing Auto-Step Behavior**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how `CampaignBannerCarousel` handles automatic stepping every 3.5 seconds using `scrollTo`. I\'m tracing the interaction of CSS `snap-x snap-mandatory` and `behavior: \'smooth\'` within `scrollTo`. Specifically, I\'m noting the strategic removal of `scroll-smooth` from the container, and the explicit use of `behavior: \'smooth\'` only for auto-step and dot-click, and `behavior: \'instant\'` for internal resets. This ensures CSS scroll-smooth never interferes with instant seamless loop resets.\n\n\n**Refining Auto-Step Logic**\n\nI\'m currently refining the auto-step logic. I\'m choosing between `setInterval` or chained `setTimeout`, focusing on clean resume behavior after user interaction. I\'m leaning towards tracking the `lastActionAtRef` within the RAF loop or timer to manage the resume delay and auto-advance efficiently. The goal is to ensure a smooth transition, waiting 1.5 seconds after a user release before resuming the banner\'s auto-scroll.\n\n\n**Analyzing Scroll Resets**\n\nI\'m now tracing the auto-step in `CampaignBannerCarousel` at Banner 3. The smooth animation is key: it goes from Banner 4 to Banner 1 (clone). The challenge is to only reset the scrollLeft *after* the smooth scroll completes, so the loop feels seamless. The `computeLoopStepTarget` function is returning the correct values, but the timing is everything. It seems that auto-step correctly resumes, but I need to make sure this is smooth and continuous.\n\n\n\n**Optimizing Banner Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on scroll resets and user interactions. I\'ve been experimenting with `scrollend` combined with a `setTimeout` fallback after `scrollTo`, aiming to maintain seamless transitions. The goal is to ensure the loop feels continuous, even with banner clicks. I\'m exploring how to prevent interruptions when users interact with the banners during the auto-scroll.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_15350191608924737172"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import { useCallback, useEffect, useRef, useState, type MouseEvent } from \'react\';\\nimport { measureCarouselGeometry } from \'../utils/carouselLoop\';\\n\\nconst DRAG_THRESHOLD_PX = 6;\\nconst RESUME_DELAY_MS = 1500;\\n\\ninterface UseCarouselInteractionOptions {\\n  originalCount: number;\\n  wrapDuringDrag?: boolean;\\n  onManualActivity?: () => void;\\n}\\n\\nexport function useCarouselInteraction({\\n  originalCount,\\n  wrapDuringDrag = false,\\n  onManualActivity,\\n}: UseCarouselInteractionOptions) {\\n  const scrollerRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement | null>(null);\\n  const isDownRef = useRef(false);\\n  const isTouchingRef = useRef(false);\\n  const isHoveredRef = useRef(false);\\n  const lastTouchTsRef = useRef(0);\\n  const startXRef = useRef(0);\\n  const startScrollRef = useRef(0);\\n  const didDragRef = useRef(false);\\n  const isAutoPausedRef = useRef(false);\\n  const resumeTimerRef = useRef<number | null>(null);\\n  const [isDragging, setIsDragging] = useState(false);\\n\\n  const clearResumeTimer = useCallback(() => {\\n    if (resumeTimerRef.current !== null) {\\n      window.clearTimeout(resumeTimerRef.current);\\n      resumeTimerRef.current = null;\\n    }\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  const pauseNow = useCallback(() => {\\n    clearResumeTimer();\\n    isAutoPausedRef.current = true;\\n  }, [clearResumeTimer]);\\n\\n  const scheduleResume = useCallback(() => {\\n    clearResumeTimer();\\n    resumeTimerRef.current = window.setTimeout(() => {\\n      resumeTimerRef.current = null;\\n      if (!isTouchingRef.current && !isHoveredRef.current && !isDownRef.current) {\\n        isAutoPausedRef.current = false;\\n      }\\n    }, RESUME_DELAY_MS);\\n  }, [clearResumeTimer]);\\n\\n  const pauseTemporarily = useCallback(() => {\\n    pauseNow();\\n    scheduleResume();\\n  }, [pauseNow, scheduleResume]);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    return () => clearResumeTimer();\\n  }, [clearResumeTimer]);\\n\\n  const handleTouchStart = useCallback(() => {\\n    lastTouchTsRef.current = Date.now();\\n    isTouchingRef.current = true;\\n    pauseNow();\\n    onManualActivity?.();\\n  }, [onManualActivity, pauseNow]);\\n\\n  const handleTouchEnd = useCallback(() => {\\n    isTouchingRef.current = false;\\n    scheduleResume();\\n  }, [scheduleResume]);\\n\\n  const handleMouseEnter = useCallback(() => {\\n    if (Date.now() - lastTouchTsRef.current < 800) return;\\n    isHoveredRef.current = true;\\n    pauseNow();\\n  }, [pauseNow]);\\n\\n  const handleMouseDown = useCallback(\\n    (event: MouseEvent<HTMLDivElement>) => {\\n      const el = scrollerRef.current;\\n      if (!el) return;\\n      isDownRef.current = true;\\n      startXRef.current = event.pageX;\\n      startScrollRef.current = el.scrollLeft;\\n      didDragRef.current = false;\\n      pauseNow();\\n      onManualActivity?.();\\n    },\\n    [onManualActivity, pauseNow],\\n  );\\n\\n  const handleMouseMove = useCallback(\\n    (event: MouseEvent<HTMLDivElement>) => {\\n      const el = scrollerRef.current;\\n      if (!isDownRef.current || !el) return;\\n      const dx = event.pageX - startXRef.current;\\n      if (Math.abs(dx) > DRAG_THRESHOLD_PX) {\\n        didDragRef.current = true;\\n        if (!isDragging) setIsDragging(true);\\n        let nextScroll = startScrollRef.current - dx;\\n        if (wrapDuringDrag) {\\n          const { loopWidth } = measureCarouselGeometry(el, originalCount);\\n          if (loopWidth > 0) {\\n            if (nextScroll >= loopWidth) {\\n              nextScroll -= loopWidth;\\n              startScrollRef.current -= loopWidth;\\n            } else if (nextScroll < 0) {\\n              nextScroll += loopWidth;\\n              startScrollRef.current += loopWidth;\\n            }\\n          }\\n        }\\n        el.scrollLeft = nextScroll;\\n      }\\n    },\\n    [isDragging, originalCount, wrapDuringDrag],\\n  );\\n\\n  const finishDrag = useCallback(() => {\\n    if (isDownRef.current || isDragging) {\\n      isDownRef.current = false;\\n      setIsDragging(false);\\n      window.setTimeout(() => {\\n        didDragRef.current = false;\\n      }, 0);\\n    }\\n  }, [isDragging]);\\n\\n  const handleMouseUp = useCallback(() => {\\n    finishDrag();\\n    if (!isHoveredRef.current && !isTouchingRef.current) {\\n      scheduleResume();\\n    }\\n  }, [finishDrag, scheduleResume]);\\n\\n  const handleMouseLeave = useCallback(() => {\\n    isHoveredRef.current = false;\\n    finishDrag();\\n    scheduleResume();\\n  }, [finishDrag, scheduleResume]);\\n\\n  const consumeDidDrag = useCallback(() => {\\n    if (!didDragRef.current) return false;\\n    didDragRef.current = false;\\n    return true;\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  return {\\n    scrollerRef,\\n    isDragging,\\n    isDownRef,\\n    isTouchingRef,\\n    isAutoPausedRef,\\n    pauseTemporarily,\\n    consumeDidDrag,\\n    containerInteractionProps: {\\n      onTouchStart: handleTouchStart,\\n      onTouchEnd: handleTouchEnd,\\n      onTouchCancel: handleTouchEnd,\\n      onMouseEnter: handleMouseEnter,\\n      onMouseLeave: handleMouseLeave,\\n      onMouseDown: handleMouseDown,\\n      onMouseMove: handleMouseMove,\\n      onMouseUp: handleMouseUp,\\n      onDragStart: (e: React.DragEvent<HTMLDivElement>) => e.preventDefault(),\\n    },\\n  };\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create shared carousel interaction hook with 6px drag threshold, touch/hover/mouse pause, and 1.5s resume delay\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/hooks/useCarouselInteraction.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating carousel interaction hook\", \"toolSummary\":\"Carousel interaction hook creation\"}"
