  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Mapping Requirements Directly**\n\nMy focus is on mapping every user requirement directly into clean, focused modules, each under 250 lines. The modular architecture is shaping up beautifully, with a perfect file mirroring. I\'m building a requirement checklist for the new architecture, so all goals will be achieved directly by well-defined functions.\n\n\n**Defining New Types**\n\nI\'ve been defining new types, specifically extending `MapLayerFilter` to include `\'police_stations\'` and adding a `PoliceStation` interface. This includes necessary details like ID, name, address, phone number, and distance. I\'ve also extended the `InspectedPlace` type to include police station data. I\'ve begun working on the police station API, with functions to fetch nearby stations, and handle the logic for using the Google Places API. I\'m taking into account the need for a Google API Key and constructing the correct POST requests with necessary parameters and field masks.\n\n\n**Implementing Fallbacks and Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing fallback logic for police station data. I\'ve integrated checks for Google API keys and network availability. If the Google Places API fails, or the device is offline, I\'m falling back to Geoapify with a similar query structure. If Geoapify also fails, I\'m constructing local \"seed\" data for several stations. This includes real phone numbers, where available, or handles the null case as explicitly requested. I\'m taking the logic for the Google Maps link for the station\'s contact number.\n\n\n**Refining Offline Fallback**\n\nI\'m revisiting the offline fallback for police station data. I\'m focusing on handling phone numbers more cleanly, ensuring I only extract real `nationalPhoneNumber` or properties. I\'ll maintain a null value if no verified number is found, rather than inventing fake numbers. For Vietnamese name normalization, I\'ll build \"Tr\341\273\245 s\341\273\237 C\303\264ng an Khu v\341\273\261c\" plus the area/street suffix if the raw name is missing or generic. Also I have added cleaning \"Ward Police\" to \"C\303\264ng an Ph\306\260\341\273\235ng\".\n\n\n**Constructing Logic Hooks**\n\nI am now focusing on building the `usePoliceStationState.ts` hook. It will mirror the `useGasStationState` structure, fetching nearby stations with `fetchNearbyPoliceStations`. This will include tracking the `policeStations`, and state variables. The logic will enable users to select, navigate to stations, and clear the selected route. I\'m also ensuring the hook addresses the specific requirement for switching to the map tab and activating the \"C\303\264ng an\" filter upon user interaction. I\'ve got to ensure distance sorting and Google Maps URLs are correct.\n\n\n**Orchestrating Police Station Routing**\n\nI\'m now integrating automated routing to the nearest police station. I\'m focusing on crafting a function, let\'s call it `openPoliceStationsMode`, which will handle cleaning routes, setting up the map, and triggering a fresh scan of nearby stations. This will involve switching to the map, setting the police station filter, resetting the step, and fetching stations with `fetchNearbyPoliceStations`. This will instantly route to the nearest station and activate the bottom sheet, without conflicting with the floating card. I am verifying the design is seamless and intuitive. The route should be indigo, to match the rest of the application.\n\n\n**Refining Map Integration**\n\nI\'m working on the map integration, specifically how the `PoliceStationListSheet` will interact with the map display. I\'m focusing on ensuring routes, markers, and the bottom sheet all display seamlessly. I\'m considering the edge case of users clicking \"\304\220\306\260\341\273\235ng \304\221i\" within the list sheet, ensuring the proper route renders without conflicts.\n\n\n**Integrating Map Markers and Routes**\n\nI\'m now integrating the map markers and routes. I\'ve added a \'police-route\' source in `mapLayers.ts` with white casing and an indigo line. I\'m building `createPoliceStationMarkerElement` in `mapMarkers.ts`, using a round badge with a shield SVG icon, and a \"G\341\272\247n nh\341\272\245t\" label for the nearest station. I\'m also implementing clicking markers to inspect police stations via a floating card with route drawing and clean fitting. I am getting the indigo OSRM route working.\n\n\n**Synchronizing Map Markers**\n\nI am now focusing on synchronizing map markers. I\'m adding `policeStations`, `policeRoute`, and `onSelectPoliceStation` to `useMapMarkersSync.ts`. Markers will render based on filter conditions and tracking state. I\'m ensuring all four marker types render correctly in the \'all\' filter mode, along with the correct fitBounds. I\'m also ensuring the active route routing to police station will use indigo and other related properties.\n\n\n**Adding Map Filters**\n\nI\'m now integrating the map filter chips. I\'ve added a \"C\303\264ng an\" chip with a Shield icon, indigo active tone, and a count badge. I\'ve also built the police bottom sheet, mirroring the gas station sheet. It features an emergency \"G\341\273\215i kh\341\272\251n c\341\272\245p 113\" button and a safety reminder. I\'m focusing on ensuring it is well under 190 lines.\n\n\n**Implementing UI Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Police Station features into the user interface, paying special attention to the scrollable list of police stations. Each entry will show the Vietnamese name, address, distance, and the real phone number (if available). The nearest station gets a \"G\341\272\247n nh\341\272\245t\" badge. I\'m focusing on those compact buttons for \"\304\220\306\260\341\273\235ng \304\221i\", \"G\341\273\215i \304\221i\341\273\207n\", and \"Google Maps\", ensuring they function as designed and correctly handle phone number availability and Google Maps integration. I am implementing the indigo OSRM route and marker highlighting. I am taking into account emergency call buttons and safety reminders.\n\n\n"
