    thinking: "**Analyzing Visuals Rigorously**\n\nI\'ve meticulously reviewed the screenshots. Screenshot 1 demonstrates seamless navigation to B\341\272\243n \304\221\341\273\223 with \"C\303\264ng an\" highlighted. The visuals are incredibly clear, prompting an in-depth critique akin to a senior product designer\'s scrutiny. I am preparing to delve into the next screenshot.\n\n\n**Examining Navigation Details**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on screenshot analysis. The indigo \"C\303\264ng an 8\" chip is significant, showing a route directly to \"\304\220\341\273\223n C\303\264ng an No.42,\" marked by an indigo Shield with \"G\341\272\247n nh\341\272\245t.\" The Emergency bar is rendered, as are sorted police stations, complete with actions. My attention is drawn to two small details in Screenshot 1, specifically: truncated text in the night reminder and the \"\304\220\341\273\223n C\303\264ng an No.42\" normalization.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Consistency**\n\nI\'m now focused on visual consistency across screenshots. The full Vietnamese night reminder, revealed by `line-clamp-2`, looks far better. I\'m also comparing Screenshot 1 with `police-pin-card.png`, noticing how cleanly the `FloatingPlaceCard` appears after clicking the indigo marker, avoiding any clipping issues. I\'ve switched to reviewing Screenshot 3, which is `map-all-4-layers.png`, and I\'m very pleased with the clean co-existence of all four marker types in \"T\341\272\245t c\341\272\243\" mode. I\'m going to polish the `PoliceStationListSheet.tsx`.\n\n\n"
