  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Component Logic**\n\nI\'m currently focused on `MapTabView.tsx` and how to optimize it. Right now, it\'s at 246 lines. Adding the `onMechanicApproaching` prop offers a chance to streamline a couple of lines, perhaps combining `useState` calls or grouping props. I\'m aiming for clean, concise code.\n\n\n**Structuring Notification System**\n\nI\'ve been working on structuring the notification system. I\'m designing the types in `/src/types/notification.ts`, including `NotificationType`, `NotificationFilterTab`, `BrowserPushPermission`, and interfaces for `AppNotification` and `TriggerNotificationInput`. I\'m also preparing `/src/utils/notificationLogic.ts` to hold helpers, with initial notifications ready to go. My aim is to keep `useRescueOrderState.ts` below 250 lines.\n\n\n**Implementing Notification Helpers**\n\nI\'m now implementing the helper functions for notifications. I\'ve defined `filterNotifications`, `countUnreadNotifications`, and methods to mark notifications as read. I\'m also working on crafting Vietnamese notification messages, specifically the `buildVoucherAppliedMessage`, and formatting the timestamp using `formatNotificationTime`. The goal is to keep things efficient. Finally, I\'ve created the `createAppNotification` and `playNotificationChime` functions. I\'m aiming for concise code that is thoroughly tested.\n\n\n"
