  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing File Sizes**\n\nI quickly checked the line counts for the new files. NotificationContext.tsx is approximately 176 lines, FloatingPushBanner.tsx is roughly 118 lines, and NotificationCenterModal.tsx is around 212 lines. I see that they are all well under the line limit.\n\n\n**Implementing Phase 3**\n\nI\'ve scoped out the implementation for Phase 3. I\'ll begin by wrapping `<App />` with `<NotificationProvider>` in `/src/main.tsx`. Next, I will add the frosted `Bell` button to `/src/components/tabs/HomeTab.tsx`, integrating the `unreadCount` and `onOpenNotifications` from `useNotifications()`. I\'ll place the button with the data-testid and badge. Finally, I\'ll update `useRescueMapMechanicOverlay.ts`, adding `onMechanicApproaching` to the useRef.\n\n\n**Refining Map Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the mechanic simulation features. I\'ve added the `onMechanicApproaching` prop to `RescueMap.tsx` and propagated it to `useRescueMapMechanicOverlay`. In `MapTabView.tsx`, where it\'s around 246 lines, I\'ll combine the state hooks for the drawers to keep the line count down. I\'m also adding `onMechanicReply` to `useMechanicSimulation.ts` to capture the mechanic\'s replies and importing the notification-related hooks into `useRescueOrderState.ts`.\n\n\n**Defining Notification Triggers**\n\nI\'ve defined the notification triggers and corresponding logic. The first trigger, `handleConfirmRescue`, now calls `requestPushPermission` on the initial order request. The second trigger, `handleDemoAdvance`, will fire when the demo advances to \'accepted\'. Finally, the third trigger, `handleMechanicApproaching`, will use a callback from `MapTabView` to trigger a notification when the mechanic is nearby.\n\n\n**Implementing Notification Triggers**\n\nI\'m expanding notification triggers. I\'ll add trigger number four, `handleMechanicArrived`, activating when transitioning to the \'arrived\' state. I\'ll also add two more. Trigger number five, `onMechanicReply`, will use `triggerNotification` in `useMechanicSimulation`. Finally, I\'ll add the sixth trigger, which will be for when a voucher is applied, using `notifyVoucherApplied`.\n\n\n**Adding Final Notification Triggers**\n\nI\'ve added the final notification triggers. Trigger number seven, `handleSelectVoucher`, now calls `triggerNotification` in `VoucherDrawerModal`, `CampaignBannerCarousel`, and `PartnerPerksCarousel`. Additionally, it integrates with `handleSelectGasStationForRescue` to show the notification. Lastly, trigger number eight, `handleQuickSos`, is a `safety` type, showing the current GPS coordinates.\n\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
